{"parentUuid":"3dec5b8c-ba67-4844-85cb-6ad2b2b72212","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01Xj62qkgjaXcGgZgfd3FWci","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"faucet-stream\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.2.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":1283},"type":"attachment","uuid":"10fab6fb-21af-4dcd-a403-1c7b8def2751","timestamp":"2026-09-17T09:42:27.758Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"10fab6fb-21af-4dcd-a403-1c7b8def2751","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14945507 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"90e132f6-58cd-4353-a30f-2b298740e63b","timestamp":"2026-09-17T09:42:27.805Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"90e132f6-58cd-4353-a30f-2b298740e63b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf8nyaCUMA6Z86aTJnqAR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Freed ~15 GB. The four remaining workstreams are still running; I'll report when they land and then run the full gate set before pushing to #656.\n\n**Answer to your question — yes, there were pending fixes, and I'm now solving all of them in #656.**\n\n**Done and tested (mine):**\n- **#654 H7 — SQL-transform validation fail-open.** It tolerated *any* error whose text contained \"batch\", so `JOIN daily_batches` against a nonexistent table was accepted and the run died on page 1. Now it registers a zero-row `batch` placeholder so table resolution genuinely happens, and excuses only the one unknowable class (columns of a page that hasn't arrived). The existing suite immediately caught a false negative in my first predicate — DuckDB words qualified-column failures differently — which is exactly why I ran it before trusting the change.\n- **#654 H8 — Postgres-CDC slot retry.** Keyed on `\"is active\"` in rendered text, so a slot named `orders_is_active` matched and a driver reword would silently remove the restart-race backoff. Now classified on **SQLSTATE 55006**, preserved by wrapping the `sqlx` error once at the boundary (via the existing `Custom` extension point) instead of stringifying it at 12 sites. Three tests that encoded the old prose-matching were rewritten to assert the typed behavior.\n- **#654 M15 — BigQuery silently rewriting identifiers.** `quote_ident` *stripped* backticks, justified as \"the schema came from BigQuery\" — but the same function quotes **user-supplied** `write.key` columns in `MERGE` predicates, so `` a`b `` became `ab` and matched a different real column. Now escapes per BigQuery's actual grammar: correct identifier, or a loud error — never a silently different one.\n\n**In flight (five parallel workstreams, ~50 files so far):** the reserved-name and `__op` deduplication (where drifting defaults would turn deletes into inserts), the four unjittered backoff copies now that `apply_jitter` is public, WebSocket's constant-backoff reconnect, ClickHouse's second-order substitution, typed classification in run-history/scheduler/parquet/GraphQL, the XML/REST decoder panic on unbalanced input, the object-verify dedup plus Azure's missing integrity fields, and the Kafka/quality doc-comment gaps.\n\n**Still deliberately not in this PR:** the 66-config `deny_unknown_fields` rollout (blocked on the `#[serde(flatten)]` tension), the vocabulary renames, and the semver rollout across 89 crates — those change users' YAML or need a policy call, and they stay in #654 with sequencing."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":428,"cache_read_input_tokens":922008,"output_tokens":907,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":428,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":907,"cache_read_input_tokens":922008,"cache_creation_input_tokens":428,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":428},"type":"message","model":null}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011Cf8nyV2g2nW1uFEXAAShU","type":"assistant","uuid":"f3bb1f26-7539-4cf4-aac1-5cdad54b0553","timestamp":"2026-09-17T09:42:44.882Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
