{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-09-17T10:09:32.654Z","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>bv4kkwuab</task-id>\n<summary>Monitor event: \"final tests+clippy for websocket/clickhouse crates\"</summary>\n<event>test result: ok. 21 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 0.04s</event>\nIf this event is something the user would act on now, send a PushNotification. Routine or benign output doesn't need one.\n</task-notification>"}
{"parentUuid":"a0444cf2-4dcb-403b-b8aa-47f1e1885bb9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf8q3DcpLEi8B7Wtsa313","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"60 files across all the audit fixes. The last two workstreams (CLI typed classification, config docs) are still running — I'll collect them, then run the complete gate set and push to #656.\n\n**Progress so far — all in the same PR as you asked:**\n\n| Finding | What changed |\n|---|---|\n| **H7** SQL-transform fail-open | Placeholder `batch` registered so table resolution happens; only the unknowable column schema is excused. The audit's exact case now fails. |\n| **H8** Postgres-CDC slot retry | SQLSTATE `55006`, preserved by wrapping `sqlx` once at the boundary instead of stringifying at 12 sites. |\n| **M15** BigQuery identifiers | Escapes instead of silently stripping — user `write.key` columns can no longer become a *different real column* in a `MERGE`. |\n| **M12** `__faucet_ovw` | One documented constant, consumed by 5 sinks; strings byte-identical (existing tests pin them). |\n| **M17** `__op` triplication | CLI now decodes straight into core's `CdcUnwrapSpec` (−55 lines); one constant. The drifted doc was corrected rather than the default set — changing that set would reclassify deletes on live pipelines, the exact corruption this finding is about. |\n| **M3** GraphQL | Typed `extensions.code`; prose no longer flips the error variant, the `batch_size: 0` hint survives as a hint. |\n| **L25** XML/REST decoder | Frame-stack `expect()`s replaced with typed errors — no panic on unbalanced untrusted input. |\n| **L27** `__unchanged_toast__` | Named constant + README explaining it reaches sinks as a real column. |\n\nTwo things worth flagging honestly: the disk filled to 100% mid-run and blocked one workstream — I've reclaimed 58 GB and verified the affected crates compile together again. And one workstream hit a clippy error in a *peer's* file (`is_multiple_of`); I fixed it and re-verified core. Cross-crate interference like that is the cost of running this many streams in parallel, which is why nothing gets pushed until the full workspace gate passes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":756,"cache_read_input_tokens":929513,"output_tokens":727,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":756,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":727,"cache_read_input_tokens":929513,"cache_creation_input_tokens":756,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":756},"type":"message","model":null}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011Cf8q38NJN5VM5D9dgCVJT","type":"assistant","uuid":"511d02bf-38ec-437d-9489-575a7472d6e9","timestamp":"2026-09-17T10:09:45.522Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
