{"parentUuid":"55d35103-2b5e-4f5f-84d4-f06d2032c81d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf8qwx1h1yNKKRXBVg9QN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HhMHXF8mDnLNPkoypCVWGo","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory\npython3 - <<'PY'\np=\"feedback_never_use_pawan_dt_identity.md\"; s=open(p).read()\nadd = '''\n**Squash-merge trailers are a second leak path.** GitHub composes the squash commit message from the PR's commits and appends `Co-authored-by:` for every distinct author, so a branch that ever held a commit from the work identity taints the merged commit body on `main` even after the branch is reauthored — and GitHub caches that suggested message when the merge box is first rendered, so a later reauthor does not clear it. This happened to #650 and #653. **Always merge with an explicit message** (`gh pr merge N --squash --subject \"<title>\" --body \"<text>\"`), never the auto-generated one, and verify after landing with `git log -1 --format='%B' origin/main | grep -i co-authored`.\n'''\nif \"Squash-merge trailers\" not in s:\n    s = s.rstrip() + \"\\n\" + add\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"memory updated\")\nPY\ngrep -c \"Squash-merge trailers\" feedback_never_use_pawan_dt_identity.md","description":"Record the squash-trailer leak path in memory"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1923,"cache_read_input_tokens":935331,"output_tokens":506,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1923,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":506,"cache_read_input_tokens