{"parentUuid":"eb7b9569-7328-4d28-bfed-627e275cc3ca","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01HhMHXF8mDnLNPkoypCVWGo","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"faucet-stream\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.2.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":416},"type":"attachment","uuid":"58c37ef4-f55b-42e3-ac84-f9acbc99c095","timestamp":"2026-09-17T10:21:37.189Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"58c37ef4-f55b-42e3-ac84-f9acbc99c095","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/feedback_never_use_pawan_dt_identity.md","snippet":"14\t- git author/committer: `PawanSikawat <pawansikawat1998@gmail.com>` — pinned in the repo-local config (`git config user.name/user.email`), which beats the global `pawan-dt` default. **Verify before committing.**\n15\t- `gh auth switch --user PawanSikawat` once, then **leave it there**. Never \"switch back\" — the old CLAUDE.md step 3 that said to revert to `pawan-dt` was exactly what caused the mis-attribution, and that instruction has been removed.\n16\t\n17\t**Why:** `pawan-dt` is a work identity that must not appear in this personal repo's history or API calls; it also 403s on `faucet-hq` and has authored zero commits on `main`.\n18\t\n19\t**How to apply:** if a commit is ever authored as `pawan-dt`, reauthor before the branch is pushed — `FILTER_BRANCH_SQUELCH_WARNING=1 git filter-branch -f --env-filter '<remap both AUTHOR and COMMITTER>' origin/main..HEAD`, verify the tree is unchanged (`git diff backup HEAD` empty), then `git push --force-with-lease` (force-push needs the user's explicit approval — the safety classifier blocks it).\n20\t\n21\tNote the GitHub account was **renamed to `pecsorabs`** (same numeric id `35492860`), so `gh auth status` and squash-merge commits may show either name — both are this account. See [[reference_gh_auth_and_git_add_gotchas]] and [[feedback_no_claude_coauthor_trailer]].\n22\t\n23\t**Squash-merge trailers are a second leak path.** GitHub composes the squash commit message from the PR's commits and appends `Co-authored-by:` for every distinct author, so a branch that ever held a commit from the work identity taints the merged commit body on `main` even after the branch is reauthored — and GitHub caches that suggested message when the merge box is first rendered, so a later reauthor does not clear it. This happened to #650 and #653. **Always merge with an explicit message** (`gh pr merge N --squash --subject \"<title>\" --body \"<text>\"`), never the auto-generated one, and verify after landing with `git log -1 --format='%B' origin/main | grep -i co-authored`."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"17cef580-1c04-455b-8d73-9327ffe29573","timestamp":"2026-09-17T10:21:37.212Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
