{"parentUuid":"a784c8a0-c0ef-418e-9f7c-dd111cca8cd5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf8qzHqbcCFEaYTYpKrk1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's exactly what's wrong, what I've already fixed, and the one decision that's yours.\n\n**What's actually in those two commits.** The *author* line on both is your account (`pecsorabs`, the renamed PawanSikawat) — my earlier reauthor held, and **zero commits on `main` are authored by the work identity.** What remains is one line in each commit's *body*:\n\n```\nCo-authored-by: pawan-dt <pawan@drivetrain.ai>\n```\n\nI scanned all of `main`: it's **exactly those two commits**, nothing older.\n\n**Why it happened — a leak path I hadn't closed.** GitHub composes the squash-merge message from the PR's commits and appends a `Co-authored-by:` line for every distinct author it finds. #653 was authored as `pawan-dt` when it merged (before the reauthor). For #650, GitHub had already cached the suggested message when the merge box was first rendered, so reauthoring the branch afterwards didn't clear it. Fixing the commit *authors* was necessary but not sufficient — the trailer is a second, independent path, and I missed it.\n\n**Closed now (no published history touched):**\n- `CLAUDE.md` documents the mechanism and mandates merging with an **explicit** `--subject`/`--body` so GitHub never auto-generates trailers, plus a post-merge verification command.\n- Same recorded in persistent memory so future sessions inherit it.\n- I re-armed **#656**'s auto-merge with an explicit message, and verified its branch has a single author (`PawanSikawat`) and zero work-identity mentions — so that merge cannot carry the trailer.\n\n**The decision I need from you.** Removing the trailer from the two commits already on `main` means **rewriting published history and force-pushing the protected default branch**. That is destructive and outward-facing, so I won't do it unilaterally. Concretely:\n\n- It rewrites 3 commits (`6433e74b`, `fd32cf08`, and `63b7aa73` which sits on top and gets a new SHA).\n- Every clone, fork, and any open PR based on `main` diverges and needs a reset.\n- `enforce_admins: false`, so your admin account can force-push without disabling branch protection.\n- The trees stay byte-identical — only the message bodies change.\n- **#656 must land first or be rebased**, since it's branched off `fd32cf08`.\n\nIf you want it gone, say so and I'll do it in that order (land #656, then rewrite, verify byte-identical trees, force-push with a lease). If you'd rather not rewrite published history, the alternative is to leave those two bodies alone — the identity is *not* in any author field, and the prevention above means no future commit can pick it up."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":372,"cache_read_input_tokens":939268,"output_tokens":893,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":372,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":939268,"cache_creation_input_tokens":372,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":372},"type":"message","model":null}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"requestId":"req_011Cf8qzCGEiCjuhhf3durGk","type":"assistant","uuid":"84936a1c-18cf-401d-9e5d-a9d1d66accb7","timestamp":"2026-09-17T10:22:13.444Z","effort":"high","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodl