semantics preserved everywhere — `apply_jitter` is used (not `backoff_with_jitter`) precisely so each connector's own ceiling wins. Tests: each crate's exact-equality backoff test became a `[0.5, 1.5)`-band assertion (incl. \"never zero\" and \"configured cap, not core's\"), plus a new `*_is_decorrelated_across_calls` test proving repeated identical inputs do not return an identical delay.\n\n## Finding 2 (#654 M6) — WebSocket reconnect now grows and is bounded\nNew pure `reconnect_delay(base, attempt)` in `crates/source/websocket/src/stream.rs` routes through `backoff_with_jitter` (base = the unchanged `reconnect_backoff` config field, which supplies the growth base; core supplies the ceiling the config lacks). Both sleep sites (connect-failure `:236`, reconnect `:378`) now compute from the existing `reconnect_attempts` counter and log the real delay. Tests: growth across attempts 0–4 within band, boundedness at attempts 30/1000/`usize::MAX` (`&gt;=30s` and `&lt;90s`), and decorrelation.\n\n## Finding 3 (#654 M14) — one ANSI escaper, one justified dialect divergence\n`faucet_core::write_mode::sql_literal` is now `pub` + re-exported from `lib.rs`, with a doc comment stating it is the ANSI escaper and that a dialect needing other rules must say so explicitly. Two new core tests cover every scalar kind, empty string, multiple quotes, non-scalars→`NULL`, and a breakout attempt.\n\n**Deliberate divergence kept:** ClickHouse must keep its own escaper. I verified against ClickHouse's syntax reference — backslash *is* a meta-character in its string literals (\"you need to escape at least `'` and `\\`\"), so ANSI quote-doubling alone is unsafe there: a value ending in `\\` emits `'foo\\'`, whose backslash eats the closing quote. `faucet_common_clickhouse::sql_literal` keeps `\\\\`/`\\'`, now with a `# Why not faucet_core::sql_literal` section naming both failure modes, plus a new test asserting exactly the inputs ANSI would mishandle (`foo\\`, `a\\'`, `x\\' OR 1=1 --`) and a property check that no backslash is left dangling.\n\n## Finding 4 (#654 M14, second-order injection) — single non-re-scanning pass\n`substitute_context_sql` no longer loops `String::replace` per context entry over its own output. Values are pre-rendered to ClickHouse literals and handed to core's audited single left-to-right scanner (`faucet_core::util::substitute_context`), which never re-scans replacement text — so no duplicated scanner logic.\n\n**I also fixed the same defect across the two substitution *kinds*.** `build_effective_query` previously substituted context first, then `@bookmark` over the result — so a context value containing `@bookmark` picked up the cursor literal and broke out of its own quotes. `@bookmark` is now normalised to a reserved `{__faucet_bookmark}` key (named consts `BOOKMARK_TOKEN`/`BOOKMARK_KEY`) on the *raw author-controlled template*, and everything is substituted in one pass. Reserved key shadows any same-named context entry.\n\n**On bind parameters** (you asked me to evaluate first): I chose escaping. ClickHouse's parameter syntax is `{name:Type}` — it requires an explicit ClickHouse type inside the placeholder. Routing the documented `{key}` grammar through it would change the user-facing token syntax *and* force per-JSON-value ClickHouse type inference (int vs float, date-like strings), i.e. a breaking config change carrying fresh mis-typing bugs. Rationale is recorded in the function's doc comment.\n\nSix new tests: no re-substitution of a value naming another key; neither direction of context↔bookmark injection; order-independence (same context built forward and reversed yields byte-identical SQL); reserved key cannot be shadowed; unmatched placeholders left verbatim.\n\n## Verification\n`cargo fmt` clean on all 9 files. Tests green: core 1170, sink-kinesis 17, sink-sqs 13, source-kinesis 19, source-grpc 22, common-clickhouse 21, source-clickhouse 34, source-websocket 27. `clippy --all-targets --all-features -D warnings` clean on all 8 crates. Index is empty; all changes are unstaged working-tree edits. No files outside my list were modified.\n\n## Two things you need to action\n\n1. **A peer agent lost work and I could not safely restore it.** I ran `git stash` to get a clean baseline for a pre-existing-failure check — a mistake with parallel agents, since it reverted *everyone's* uncommitted work. I recovered 24 files from the stash (mine and peers'). For the other 12, peers had already re-edited them, so I left their live versions alone. Eleven of those twelve lost nothing, but **`crates/source/postgres-cdc/src/replication.rs` has 95 lines in the stash that are absent from the current file** (stash: +103/−31; current: +1/−1, a newer edit not in the stash — the two diverge, so I did not merge). The stash entry **`stash@{0}` is intentionally retained**; that agent can recover with `git checkout stash@{0} -- crates/source/postgres-cdc/src/replication.rs` (which would drop its newer one-line `slot_in_use()` change) or diff against the copy I saved at `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f/scratchpad/replication.rs.stashed`. Please don't drop that stash until they've looked.\n\n2. **A docs-sync follow-up outside my file list.** The WebSocket `reconnect_backoff` semantics changed from constant to exponential base, so three places now read wrong and I was scoped out of editing them: `crates/source/websocket/src/config.rs:70` (\"Fixed wait (seconds) between reconnect attempts\" — this doc comment becomes `faucet schema` output), and `crates/source/websocket/README.md` lines 16, 87, and 296 (\"fixed `reconnect_backoff`\" / \"Fixed wait between reconnect attempts\" / \"waits `reconnect_backoff`\").\n\nAlso worth knowing: the shared disk hit 0 bytes mid-run and corrupted build artifacts for every agent. I reclaimed ~1GB of `target/**/incremental` (sanctioned as safe in the maintenance rules) and ran `cargo clean -p` on the 8 packages reporting corrupted rlibs/build scripts; disk is now ~60Gi free. The `conformance_capabilities_truthful` test failure in `faucet-sink-kinesis` and `faucet-sink-sqs` is **pre-existing** — I confirmed it fails at HEAD with my changes stashed, and another agent is editing those crates' `config.rs` and `README.md`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>417322</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>474</tool_uses><duration_ms>4504820</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"parentUuid":"43df5a17-015f-4abd-aab3-c3bc7e16e54d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ab6fa6999782a78d5</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_017a17dYCSjd8vpj1sLnZPEf</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/2e42fef2-d7da-4f6e-97b1-064e451b2570/tasks/ab6fa6999782a78d5.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Dedupe backoff + SQL escaping\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All four findings are fixed, all gates green, changes left unstaged in the working tree.\n\n## Finding 1 (#654 M13) — four unjittered backoff copies deduped onto core\n\n| File | Before | After |\n|---|---|---|\n| `crates/sink/kinesis/src/sink.rs:33` | local `backoff_delay`, no jitter | keeps configured `initial_ms`/`max_ms` exponential, delegates jitter to `faucet_core::retry::apply_jitter` |\n| `crates/sink/sqs/src/sink.rs:31` | byte-identical copy | same |\n| `crates/source/kinesis/src/shard.rs:22,30` | `backoff_delay` + `jitter_fraction` (fixed 0–25% per-shard hash) | `jitter_fraction` **deleted**; `backoff_delay` caps at a named `MAX_BACKOFF` (30s) then `apply_jitter`. The old fraction was constant per shard, so after one shared throttle all shards still retried inside the same narrow window in fixed order — it never broke a herd |\n| `crates/source/grpc/src/stream.rs:786` | `next_backoff(current, cap)` doubler + `mut backoff` state | `next_backoff` **deleted**, replaced by pure `reconnect_delay(base, cap, attempt)`; the `mut backoff` variable is gone (derived from the existing `attempt` counter, so the two can no longer drift). Honours the configured `reconnect_max_backoff`, not core's 60s |\n\nConfigured base/cap semantics preserved everywhere — `apply_jitter` is used (not `backoff_with_jitter`) precisely so each connector's own ceiling wins. Tests: each crate's exact-equality backoff test became a `[0.5, 1.5)`-band assertion (incl. \"never zero\" and \"configured cap, not core's\"), plus a new `*_is_decorrelated_across_calls` test proving repeated identical inputs do not return an identical delay.\n\n## Finding 2 (#654 M6) — WebSocket reconnect now grows and is bounded\nNew pure `reconnect_delay(base, attempt)` in `crates/source/websocket/src/stream.rs` routes through `backoff_with_jitter` (base = the unchanged `reconnect_backoff` config field, which supplies the growth base; core supplies the ceiling the config lacks). Both sleep sites (connect-failure `:236`, reconnect `:378`) now compute from the existing `reconnect_attempts` counter and log the real delay. Tests: growth across attempts 0–4 within band, boundedness at attempts 30/1000/`usize::MAX` (`&gt;=30s` and `&lt;90s`), and decorrelation.\n\n## Finding 3 (#654 M14) — one ANSI escaper, one justified dialect divergence\n`faucet_core::write_mode::sql_literal` is now `pub` + re-exported from `lib.rs`, with a doc comment stating it is the ANSI escaper and that a dialect needing other rules must say so explicitly. Two new core tests cover every scalar kind, empty string, multiple quotes, non-scalars→`NULL`, and a breakout attempt.\n\n**Deliberate divergence kept:** ClickHouse must keep its own escaper. I verified against ClickHouse's syntax reference — backslash *is* a meta-character in its string literals (\"you need to escape at least `'` and `\\`\"), so ANSI quote-doubling alone is unsafe there: a value ending in `\\` emits `'foo\\'`, whose backslash eats the closing quote. `faucet_common_clickhouse::sql_literal` keeps `\\\\`/`\\'`, now with a `# Why not faucet_core::sql_literal` section naming both failure modes, plus a new test asserting exactly the inputs ANSI would mishandle (`foo\\`, `a\\'`, `x\\' OR 1=1 --`) and a property check that no backslash is left dangling.\n\n## Finding 4 (#654 M14, second-order injection) — single non-re-scanning pass\n`substitute_context_sql` no longer loops `String::replace` per context entry over its own output. Values are pre-rendered to ClickHouse literals and handed to core's audited single left-to-right scanner (`faucet_core::util::substitute_context`), which never re-scans replacement text — so no duplicated scanner logic.\n\n**I also fixed the same defect across the two substitution *kinds*.** `build_effective_query` previously substituted context first, then `@bookmark` over the result — so a context value containing `@bookmark` picked up the cursor literal and broke out of its own quotes. `@bookmark` is now normalised to a reserved `{__faucet_bookmark}` key (named consts `BOOKMARK_TOKEN`/`BOOKMARK_KEY`) on the *raw author-controlled template*, and everything is substituted in one pass. Reserved key shadows any same-named context entry.\n\n**On bind parameters** (you asked me to evaluate first): I chose escaping. ClickHouse's parameter syntax is `{name:Type}` — it requires an explicit ClickHouse type inside the placeholder. Routing the documented `{key}` grammar through it would change the user-facing token syntax *and* force per-JSON-value ClickHouse type inference (int vs float, date-like strings), i.e. a breaking config change carrying fresh mis-typing bugs. Rationale is recorded in the function's doc comment.\n\nSix new tests: no re-substitution of a value naming another key; neither direction of context↔bookmark injection; order-independence (same context built forward and reversed yields byte-identical SQL); reserved key cannot be shadowed; unmatched placeholders left verbatim.\n\n## Verification\n`cargo fmt` clean on all 9 files. Tests green: core 1170, sink-kinesis 17, sink-sqs 13, source-kinesis 19, source-grpc 22, common-clickhouse 21, source-clickhouse 34, source-websocket 27. `clippy --all-targets --all-features -D warnings` clean on all 8 crates. Index is empty; all changes are unstaged working-tree edits. No files outside my list were modified.\n\n## Two things you need to action\n\n1. **A peer agent lost work and I could not safely restore it.** I ran `git stash` to get a clean baseline for a pre-existing-failure check — a mistake with parallel agents, since it reverted *everyone's* uncommitted work. I recovered 24 files from the stash (mine and peers'). For the other 12, peers had already re-edited them, so I left their live versions alone. Eleven of those twelve lost nothing, but **`crates/source/postgres-cdc/src/replication.rs` has 95 lines in the stash that are absent from the current file** (stash: +103/−31; current: +1/−1, a newer edit not in the stash — the two diverge, so I did not merge). The stash entry **`stash@{0}` is intentionally retained**; that agent can recover with `git checkout stash@{0} -- crates/source/postgres-cdc/src/replication.rs` (which would drop its newer one-line `slot_in_use()` change) or diff against the copy I saved at `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f/scratchpad/replication.rs.stashed`. Please don't drop that stash until they've looked.\n\n2. **A docs-sync follow-up outside my file list.** The WebSocket `reconnect_backoff` semantics changed from constant to exponential base, so three places now read wrong and I was scoped out of editing them: `crates/source/websocket/src/config.rs:70` (\"Fixed wait (seconds) between reconnect attempts\" — this doc comment becomes `faucet schema` output), and `crates/source/websocket/README.md` lines 16, 87, and 296 (\"fixed `reconnect_backoff`\" / \"Fixed wait between reconnect attempts\" / \"waits `reconnect_backoff`\").\n\nAlso worth knowing: the shared disk hit 0 bytes mid-run and corrupted build artifacts for every agent. I reclaimed ~1GB of `target/**/incremental` (sanctioned as safe in the maintenance rules) and ran `cargo clean -p` on the 8 packages reporting corrupted rlibs/build scripts; disk is now ~60Gi free. The `conformance_capabilities_truthful` test failure in `faucet-sink-kinesis` and `faucet-sink-sqs` is **pre-existing** — I confirmed it fails at HEAD with my changes stashed, and another agent is editing those crates' `config.rs` and `README.md`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>417322</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>474</tool_uses><duration_ms>4504820</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","commandMode":"task-notification","timestamp":"2026-09-17T10:30:43.595Z"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"55368d5c-492f-4f9b-814a-aa8363890d12","timestamp":"2026-09-17T10:30:43.595Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"55368d5c-492f-4f9b-814a-aa8363890d12","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"32","subject":"PR-prep sweep + docs for #633 (awaiting user go)","description":"Before opening PR #633: full workspace clippy (--workspace --all-targets, touch changed files first) + tests (faucet-core, faucet-source-rest, faucet-sink-bigquery) + patch coverage; docs — cookbook/reference for native byte-passthrough + JSON logging note; maintenance docs-sync surfaces; connectors.md/architecture.md notes. No commits/PR until user says done. Fork: user may want Arrow columnar (#635) first.","activeForm":"Prepping #633 PR sweep + docs","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"33","subject":"Clean concurrency re-sweep (6/8/10) after Meltano sync done — ON HOLD","description":"HOLD on all Salesforce/BQ runs to conserve credits/quota. The mc=8 wall-time varied 18.7↔22.1 min — attributed to a concurrent Meltano full sync contending for the shared lexipol org's Bulk API. Once Meltano's sync completes, re-run the concurrency sweep (6/8/10 at 50k) in the uncontended org to get a clean comparison. Memory result is robust regardless (~140-185MB flat). Do NOT trigger until user confirms Meltano is done.","activeForm":"Holding for clean concurrency re-sweep","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"34","subject":"#630: incremental replication for Salesforce Bulk / async_job","description":"Inject WHERE <replication_key> > <bookmark> into the submit SOQL (clause-aware); emit run-start timestamp as the new bookmark (native-compatible, no data parse); wire into both stream_pages_inner (Value path) and stream_native (#633). Reuse replication_method/replication_key/start_replication_value/runtime_start. Pure SOQL-injection helper + wiremock tests. Composes with write_mode upsert for a true mirror.","activeForm":"Implementing #630 incremental Salesforce Bulk","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"35","subject":"#639: lineage/catalog samplers preserve native fast path","description":"SamplingSource/SamplingSink forward native_output_formats/stream_native + native_load_capabilities/load_native with a tap that samples a bounded NDJSON prefix while passing bytes through unchanged. Add unit tests; rebuild catalog binary; re-run Salesforce catalog test to confirm native path selected (memory ~150MB) with datasets still recorded.","activeForm":"Fixing #639 native-path regression in samplers","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"36","subject":"Fix CI: merge main + regenerate committed schema (notifications drift)","description":"Test/Coverage fail on committed_schema_covers_current_build: /properties/notifications missing — main moved (notify block). Merge origin/main into feat/native-byte-passthrough-633, regenerate schemas/faucet.schema.json feature-complete (arrow/compression/encryption), title-merge onto main's committed baseline, verify subset test passes.","activeForm":"Fixing committed-schema CI failure","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"37","subject":"Core native-path fixes (review H1–H4, M1)","description":"pipeline.rs/native.rs: (H1) gate quality/contract/masking/DLQ unconditionally in core, remove waivable requires_passthrough/forbids_dlq; (H2) native overwrite atomicity — no flush on cancel, no mid-run bookmark flush under overwrite, single finalize at successful end; (H3) reject native when sink.dedups_by_key() (upsert/delete) at core level, document invariant; (H4) respect suppress_overwrite_lifecycle in native negotiation; (M1) planner hard-rejects ExactlyOnce in NativePrerequisites.delivery. Add unit tests for each disqualifier + bookmark persist + cancel path (M5).","activeForm":"Fixing core native-path review findings","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"38","subject":"REST async-job fixes (review H1–H4, M1/M2, M5–M7)","description":"(H1) token_endpoint: classify transient 400 by parsed OAuth `error` code (typed RFC 6749 field), not body substring grep; (H2) validate gate: incremental+async_job requires amendable submit query (else Config error), don't emit bookmark when predicate not injected; (H3) honor replication_bind on async-job path / document the query-field convention, rename soql_*→sql_* identifiers; (H4) subtract lookback margin from client-clock bookmark (reuse window.lookback shape); (M1) token retry via shared runner w/ jitter; (M2) wrap submit/poll/fetch in retry::execute_with_retry; (M5) stable_short_hash → faucet_core::shard::shard_hash; (M6) dataset_uri sobjects/→objects/; (M7) state key rest-incremental → derive from dataset_uri. Tests for injected predicate over the wire + trailing bookmark + stream_native.","activeForm":"Fixing REST async-job review findings","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"39","subject":"CLI/serve fixes (review H1/H2, M1–M7, L2/L3)","description":"(H1) /v1/runs status filter: 422 on unparseable token instead of silent unfiltered; (H2) multi-status list tests on sqlite+postgres + RunStatus::parse round-trip test; (M1) cfg(unix) memstat + target-gated libc + extracted normalize_maxrss w/ tests; (M2) scope name/name_snake/name_lower/field_names check_refs exemption to discovery-bearing configs; (M3) document max_concurrent:0 sentinel in doc comment; (M4) UI document-listener teardown in runs.js/datasets.js; (M5) openapi.yaml status param → comma-separated; (M6) timeout around resolve_dynamic_fanout in serve load + fix stale comment; (M7) dedupe fmtInt in datasets.js; (L2) describe_gauge for peak-RSS + architecture.md metrics list; (L3) add pending/sharded to console STATUSES.","activeForm":"Fixing CLI/serve review findings","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"40","subject":"Docs sync for review findings (poll backoff, async-job incremental, native)","description":"REST M4/L4: poll.interval_secs doc comment + README (backoff-to-cap semantics); README async-job incremental + native passthrough sections; token_endpoint encoding field in README auth table; Sink::load_native trait docs (empty-payload no-op contract); docs/book pages for new discovery/partition surfaces per maintenance.md.","activeForm":"Syncing docs for review findings","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"41","subject":"Raise coverage floor to 95% + close PR 650's patch-coverage gap","description":"User directive: >=95% patch coverage always. Policy updated (ci.yml --min 95, codecov.yml, PRINCIPLES.md, CLAUDE.md, memory). PR 650 measured 87.41% (3637/4161; 524 uncovered changed lines — CI printed first 40: dynamic_fanout.rs 27-124, executor.rs 731/2495-2496). Running local llvm-cov (core/lineage/rest/bigquery done in bg, then cli) + scripts/patch-coverage.py --min 95 to get full list; write tests until >=95%; push.","activeForm":"Closing the patch-coverage gap to ≥95%","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"42","subject":"Whole-project principles audit (P1–P10) + report","description":"User asked for a project-wide evaluation against PRINCIPLES.md. 4 read-only agents auditing P1/P8 (vendor leakage), P2/P5 (duplication + hidden state), P6/P3 (typed errors + semver), P4/P10 (config API + docs sync). P7 measured by me: structural test presence healthy (4812 test fns, 90 crates, zero untested crates; earlier 0% readings were a measurement artifact of running only 5 crate suites). Already fixed my own P10 drift: patch-coverage.py default + failure message 90→95, docs/contributing/testing.md (also corrected a false \"codecov/patch is required\" claim), docs/architecture-review.md. Open question to raise: codecov project target now 95% but true workspace total is unmeasured (~85-90% historically) — recommend patch=95 enforced + project=auto/threshold rather than an unreachable number.","activeForm":"Auditing the project against PRINCIPLES.md","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}],"itemCount":11},"type":"attachment","uuid":"affb4578-7254-4582-b65b-