{"parentUuid":"8d3840d4-5b01-47fe-8975-635601fc0eef","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"task_reminder","content":[{"id":"32","subject":"PR-prep sweep + docs for #633 (awaiting user go)","description":"Before opening PR #633: full workspace clippy (--workspace --all-targets, touch changed files first) + tests (faucet-core, faucet-source-rest, faucet-sink-bigquery) + patch coverage; docs — cookbook/reference for native byte-passthrough + JSON logging note; maintenance docs-sync surfaces; connectors.md/architecture.md notes. No commits/PR until user says done. Fork: user may want Arrow columnar (#635) first.","activeForm":"Prepping #633 PR sweep + docs","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"33","subject":"Clean concurrency re-sweep (6/8/10) after Meltano sync done — ON HOLD","description":"HOLD on all Salesforce/BQ runs to conserve credits/quota. The mc=8 wall-time varied 18.7↔22.1 min — attributed to a concurrent Meltano full sync contending for the shared lexipol org's Bulk API. Once Meltano's sync completes, re-run the concurrency sweep (6/8/10 at 50k) in the uncontended org to get a clean comparison. Memory result is robust regardless (~140-185MB flat). Do NOT trigger until user confirms Meltano is done.","activeForm":"Holding for clean concurrency re-sweep","status":"pending","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"34","subject":"#630: incremental replication for Salesforce Bulk / async_job","description":"Inject WHERE <replication_key> > <bookmark> into the submit SOQL (clause-aware); emit run-start timestamp as the new bookmark (native-compatible, no data parse); wire into both stream_pages_inner (Value path) and stream_native (#633). Reuse replication_method/replication_key/start_replication_value/runtime_start. Pure SOQL-injection helper + wiremock tests. Composes with write_mode upsert for a true mirror.","activeForm":"Implementing #630 incremental Salesforce Bulk","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"35","subject":"#639: lineage/catalog samplers preserve native fast path","description":"SamplingSource/SamplingSink forward native_output_formats/stream_native + native_load_capabilities/load_native with a tap that samples a bounded NDJSON prefix while passing bytes through unchanged. Add unit tests; rebuild catalog binary; re-run Salesforce catalog test to confirm native path selected (memory ~150MB) with datasets still recorded.","activeForm":"Fixing #639 native-path regression in samplers","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"36","subject":"Fix CI: merge main + regenerate committed schema (notifications drift)","description":"Test/Coverage fail on committed_schema_covers_current_build: /properties/notifications missing — main moved (notify block). Merge origin/main into feat/native-byte-passthrough-633, regenerate schemas/faucet.schema.json feature-complete (arrow/compression/encryption), title-merge onto main's committed baseline, verify subset test passes.","activeForm":"Fixing committed-schema CI failure","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"37","subject":"Core native-path fixes (review H1–H4, M1)","description":"pipeline.rs/native.rs: (H1) gate quality/contract/masking/DLQ unconditionally in core, remove waivable requires_passthrough/forbids_dlq; (H2) native overwrite atomicity — no flush on cancel, no mid-run bookmark flush under overwrite, single finalize at successful end; (H3) reject native when sink.dedups_by_key() (upsert/delete) at core level, document invariant; (H4) respect suppress_overwrite_lifecycle in native negotiation; (M1) planner hard-rejects ExactlyOnce in NativePrerequisites.delivery. Add unit tests for each disqualifier + bookmark persist + cancel path (M5).","activeForm":"Fixing core native-path review findings","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"38","subject":"REST async-job fixes (review H1–H4, M1/M2, M5–M7)","description":"(H1) token_endpoint: classify transient 400 by parsed OAuth `error` code (typed RFC 6749 field), not body substring grep; (H2) validate gate: incremental+async_job requires amendable submit query (else Config error), don't emit bookmark when predicate not injected; (H3) honor replication_bind on async-job path / document the query-field convention, rename soql_*→sql_* identifiers; (H4) subtract lookback margin from client-clock bookmark (reuse window.lookback shape); (M1) token retry via shared runner w/ jitter; (M2) wrap submit/poll/fetch in retry::execute_with_retry; (M5) stable_short_hash → faucet_core::shard::shard_hash; (M6) dataset_uri sobjects/→objects/; (M7) state key rest-incremental → derive from dataset_uri. Tests for injected predicate over the wire + trailing bookmark + stream_native.","activeForm":"Fixing REST async-job review findings","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"39","subject":"CLI/serve fixes (review H1/H2, M1–M7, L2/L3)","description":"(H1) /v1/runs status filter: 422 on unparseable token instead of silent unfiltered; (H2) multi-status list tests on sqlite+postgres + RunStatus::parse round-trip test; (M1) cfg(unix) memstat + target-gated libc + extracted normalize_maxrss w/ tests; (M2) scope name/name_snake/name_lower/field_names check_refs exemption to discovery-bearing configs; (M3) document max_concurrent:0 sentinel in doc comment; (M4) UI document-listener teardown in runs.js/datasets.js; (M5) openapi.yaml status param → comma-separated; (M6) timeout around resolve_dynamic_fanout in serve load + fix stale comment; (M7) dedupe fmtInt in datasets.js; (L2) describe_gauge for peak-RSS + architecture.md metrics list; (L3) add pending/sharded to console STATUSES.","activeForm":"Fixing CLI/serve review findings","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"40","subject":"Docs sync for review findings (poll backoff, async-job incremental, native)","description":"REST M4/L4: poll.interval_secs doc comment + README (backoff-to-cap semantics); README async-job incremental + native passthrough sections; token_endpoint encoding field in README auth table; Sink::load_native trait docs (empty-payload no-op contract); docs/book pages for new discovery/partition surfaces per maintenance.md.","activeForm":"Syncing docs for review findings","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"41","subject":"Raise coverage floor to 95% + close PR 650's patch-coverage gap","description":"User directive: >=95% patch coverage always. Policy updated (ci.yml --min 95, codecov.yml, PRINCIPLES.md, CLAUDE.md, memory). PR 650 measured 87.41% (3637/4161; 524 uncovered changed lines — CI printed first 40: dynamic_fanout.rs 27-124, executor.rs 731/2495-2496). Running local llvm-cov (core/lineage/rest/bigquery done in bg, then cli) + scripts/patch-coverage.py --min 95 to get full list; write tests until >=95%; push.","activeForm":"Closing the patch-coverage gap to ≥95%","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]},{"id":"42","subject":"Whole-project principles audit (P1–P10) + report","description":"User asked for a project-wide evaluation against PRINCIPLES.md. 4 read-only agents auditing P1/P8 (vendor leakage), P2/P5 (duplication + hidden state), P6/P3 (typed errors + semver), P4/P10 (config API + docs sync). P7 measured by me: structural test presence healthy (4812 test fns, 90 crates, zero untested crates; earlier 0% readings were a measurement artifact of running only 5 crate suites). Already fixed my own P10 drift: patch-coverage.py default + failure message 90→95, docs/contributing/testing.md (also corrected a false \"codecov/patch is required\" claim), docs/architecture-review.md. Open question to raise: codecov project target now 95% but true workspace total is unmeasured (~85-90% historically) — recommend patch=95 enforced + project=auto/threshold rather than an unreachable number.","activeForm":"Auditing the project against PRINCIPLES.md","status":"completed","blocks":[],"blockedBy":[]}],"itemCount":11},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d55ff6c1-f4db-4838-af17-