{"parentUuid":"94112db4-c69c-4895-87ba-5b22a6a26107","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"91312dea-16e7-4274-81b7-7d6b5175e752","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. **Primary Request and Intent:**\n\n   This session continued work on `faucet-stream` (Rust monorepo, 92 crates). The user's explicit requests, in order:\n\n   - **\"Now tell me, have you done a review of the whole PR, and is there anything that you would change?\"** — Requested an honest assessment of whether PR #650 had been fully reviewed.\n   - **\"ci failed on test coverage. can you please ensure always that we follow atleat 95% test coverage\"** — Raise the coverage standard to ≥95% permanently and fix the failing gate.\n   - **\"the commits are comming from pawan-dt. please dont do that\"** followed by **\"Don't ever use the Pawan-DT git account on this repo. I'm being very, very clear. It should always use the other ID. I can't be more serious about it. Please don't ever use that.\"** — ABSOLUTE constraint on git/GitHub identity.\n   - **\"Yes, please do the push.\"** — Approval for the single force-push needed to publish reauthored history.\n   - **\"why is this 21k lines of code now? it was 10k earlier\"** — Explain/fix PR diff size inflation.\n   - **\"based on the new principles we defined, evaluate the whole project and check whether there are any improvement areas or something we should fix\"** — Whole-project audit against PRINCIPLES.md.\n   - **\"you are the expert, wear an expert hat and a expert maintainer of this world class repo. take the right call which you should be certain about and do it\"** — Autonomy to fix what I'm certain about.\n   - **\"Are there any fixes which are pending right now that you should solve?\"** + mid-turn **\"Please solve all of them in the same PR issues.\"** — Fix all remaining audit items in the same PR (#656).\n   - Two commit URLs + **\"Both these commits have Pawan's detail inside them.\"** + **\"pawan-dt\"** — Identify/remove the work identity from merged commits.\n\n   **Security/constraint instructions that MUST remain in force (verbatim intent):**\n   - \"Don't ever use the Pawan-DT git account on this repo... It should always use the other ID.\" Applies to commits, `gh` commands, and pushes. Correct identity: `PawanSikawat <pawansikawat1998@gmail.com>`; GitHub account renamed to `pecsorabs` (id 35492860).\n   - No `Co-Authored-By: Claude` trailer in this repo.\n   - Never use employer/customer/tenant identifiers (e.g. \"Drivetrain\") in public repo artifacts; that rule lives in local memory only, never in tracked files.\n   - \"Adding an API should not bump the version\" — never bump a major unilaterally.\n   - ≥95% patch coverage is a hard floor.\n   - Auto-merge on #650 was to stay off until the user approved (since merged by the user).\n\n2. **Key Technical Concepts:**\n   - PRINCIPLES.md P1–P10: vendor test, correctness-lives-once-in-core, extension points/semver contract, config-is-an-API, no hidden state/magic strings, typed errors (never message-grep), pure-core+tested, one vocabulary, found-in-review-fixed-before-merge, docs-move-with-code\n   - Declared semver contract via `[package.metadata.cargo-semver-checks.lints]` (`constructible_struct_adds_field`, `constructible_struct_adds_private_field`, `enum_struct_variant_field_added` = allow)\n   - Patch-coverage gate: `scripts/patch-coverage.py --lcov --base origin/main --min 95` inside the required `Coverage` job (codecov/patch is NOT required and posts unreliably)\n   - `cargo llvm-cov --no-report` per crate + `report --lcov` with an ignore regex\n   - Toolchain pinning: Homebrew rustc shadows rustup → must set `RUSTC=~/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin/rustc` and use that dir's cargo\n   - `DOCKER_HOST=unix://$HOME/.colima/default/docker.sock` for testcontainers; SQL Server image is x86-only (CI-only on ARM Mac)\n   - Generated-schema key-order phantom diffs; splice generated content in main's key order\n   - GitHub squash-merge injects `Co-authored-by` trailers from commit authors and caches the suggested message\n\n3. **Files and Code Sections:**\n\n   - **`crates/core/src/pipeline.rs`** — Core retry gate (#654 C1, the most serious finding). `with_retry_write!` gated on `supports_idempotent_writes()`, which only promises rows+token atomicity on the *idempotent* path; 11 sinks return true while their plain write is a multi-row INSERT, so the macro retried exactly what its own comment forbade. Changed gate to `sink.write_batch_is_replay_safe()`. Also: native overwrite now flushes exactly once (terminal), holds bookmarks under overwrite, returns without flushing on cancel; value path skips terminal flush for a cancelled overwrite; native scope derives from the state key.\n   - **`crates/core/src/traits.rs`** — Added defaulted `fn write_batch_is_replay_safe(&self) -> bool { self.dedups_by_key() }` with extensive doc explaining why it is NOT `supports_idempotent_writes`. Removed `NativePrerequisites` references; documented `load_native` empty-payload no-op + atomic-overwrite contracts.\n   - **`crates/core/src/native.rs`** — Deleted `NativePrerequisites`; `NativeLoadCapability` is now `{format, mechanism, write_modes}`; `plan_native_transfer` applies unconditional pipeline-owned gates (transforms/governance/DLQ/exactly-once).\n   - **`crates/core/src/error.rs`** — `FaucetError` now `#[non_exhaustive]` (#654 H11).\n   - **`crates/core/src/retry.rs`** — `apply_jitter` made `pub` (#654 M13) so connectors stop copying it.\n   - **`crates/core/src/write_mode.rs`** — `sql_literal` made pub (agent); I fixed clippy `is_multiple_of` in its test.\n   - **`crates/core/src/quality/config.rs`**, **`cli/src/config.rs`** — `deny_unknown_fields` added to quality specs + the 4 observability structs (#654 M18).\n   - **`crates/source/rest/src/auth/token_endpoint.rs`** — Typed OAuth transience: `TRANSIENT_OAUTH_ERROR_CODES = &[\"server_error\",\"temporarily_unavailable\",\"unknown_error\"]`, classified from the parsed `error` member, never `error_description`; backoff delegates to `faucet_core::retry::backoff_with_jitter`.\n   - **`crates/source/rest/src/stream.rs`** — `top_level_tokens` (paren/quote-aware), `inject_sql_predicate`, `sql_literal`, `sql_from_object`, `is_sql_datetime` (renamed from soql_*); `async_job_new_bookmark` subtracts `job.lookback_duration()` and returns None without an amendable query; `job_request_bytes`/`job_request_response` retry via `retry::execute_with_retry`; dataset URI uses `objects/` + `faucet_core::shard::shard_hash`; state key `rest:{hash}` from dataset identity.\n   - **`crates/source/rest/src/async_job.rs`** — Added `lookback` field, `supports_incremental_query()`, `lookback_duration()`, `DEFAULT_BOOKMARK_LOOKBACK_SECS = 300`; poll `interval_secs` doc corrected to backoff-cap semantics.\n   - **`crates/source/rest/tests/native_and_discovery.rs`** (new, 17 tests) — wiremock coverage of `stream_native`, OData discovery/partitioning, discovery recipe.\n   - **`crates/transform-sql/src/compile.rs`** (#654 H7) — Replaced fail-open validation with placeholder registration + narrow predicate:\n     ```rust\n     fn is_column_resolution_error(msg: &str) -> bool {\n         let m = msg.to_ascii_lowercase();\n         m.contains(\"referenced column\")\n             || m.contains(\"does not have a column named\")\n             || (m.contains(\"binder error\") && m.contains(\"group by\"))\n     }\n     ```\n     `validate_query` now runs `CREATE OR REPLACE TEMP TABLE \"batch\" AS SELECT NULL AS __faucet_placeholder WHERE 1=0;` before `conn.prepare`.\n   - **`crates/transform-sql/tests/runtime.rs`** — 4 new tests incl. `validation_rejects_a_genuinely_missing_table` (the audit's exact `daily_batches` case).\n   - **`crates/source/postgres-cdc/src/replication.rs`** (#654 H8) — Added `SQLSTATE_OBJECT_IN_USE = \"55006\"`, `PostgresError { sqlstate, context, message }` (thiserror, carried in `FaucetError::Custom`), `PostgresError::new`, `pg_err(context, sqlx::Error)`, `sqlstate_of`; `is_slot_active_error` now `sqlstate_of(err) == Some(SQLSTATE_OBJECT_IN_USE)`; 12 sqlx sites routed through `pg_err` (2 PgWireError sites reverted). **This file was lost to an agent's `git stash` and recovered from `stash@{0}`.**\n   - **`crates/sink/bigquery/src/idempotent.rs`** (#654 M15) — `quote_ident` now escapes instead of stripping: `format!(\"`{}`\", name.replace('\\\\', \"\\\\\\\\\").replace('`', \"\\\\`\"))`.\n   - **`crates/sink/mssql/src/sink.rs`** (#654 C4) — Replaced 7-substring `is_transient_error` with typed `ChunkFailure { RolledBack, Infrastructure, RowRejected }`, `AZURE_TRANSIENT`, pure `classify_server_code(u32)`, `classify_chunk_failure(&tiberius::error::Error)`, `ChunkError { class, err }` + bidirectional `From` impls, `quote_columns` (pure); re-run restricted to 1205/1222 with core's jittered backoff.\n   - **`crates/common/delta/src/connection.rs`** (#654 C2) — `is_missing_table` now typed: `matches!(e, DeltaTableError::ObjectStore { source: deltalake::ObjectStoreError::NotFound { .. } })`; new `missing_table_tests` module incl. the 403-must-not-match case.\n   - **`crates/sink/spanner/src/sink.rs`** (#654 C3) — Deleted the message-grep arm below the typed `Code::NotFound` check.\n   - **`crates/sink/http/src/sink.rs`** (#654 H5) — Added `RETRY_BASE`, pure `retry_wait(err, attempt)` (Retry-After wins, else jittered backoff), `retry_delay`; unified the two duplicated retry arms into one path.\n   - **`crates/source/clickhouse/src/stream.rs`** (#654 H6) — `default_state_key` uses `faucet_core::shard::shard_hash` instead of `DefaultHasher`.\n   - **`crates/source/s3|gcs|azure-blob/src/config.rs`** — I **reverted** an agent's `#[serde(flatten)] pub verify: ObjectVerifySpec` back to plain `pub verify_length` / `pub verify_checksum` fields (with unified canonical docs documenting both skip conditions) because removing public fields required a major bump; added `default_true()` to each crate. Verified `cargo semver-checks` → \"no semver update required\".\n   - **`.github/workflows/ci.yml`, `codecov.yml`, `PRINCIPLES.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `scripts/patch-coverage.py`, `docs/contributing/testing.md`, `docs/architecture-review.md`** — coverage floor 90→95 everywhere; testing.md's false \"codecov/patch is a required check\" claim corrected.\n   - **`.claude/rules/architecture.md`** — Added the `## Vocabulary` section (14 verbs + 3 named collisions) that PRINCIPLES.md §8 referenced but which did not exist.\n   - **`CLAUDE.md`** — Replaced \"GitHub Auth Switching\" with \"GitHub Identity — PawanSikawat only, never pawan-dt\", plus a new section on squash-merge `Co-authored-by` trailer injection and mandatory explicit `--subject`/`--body`.\n   - **Memory files** — `feedback_never_use_pawan_dt_identity.md` (new), `feedback_enforce_90_patch_coverage.md` (updated to 95%), `reference_gh_auth_and_git_add_gotchas.md` (corrected).\n\n4. **Errors and fixes:**\n   - **CI `committed_schema_covers_current_build` stale (twice)**: first missing `/properties/notifications`, then `RecordCheck/oneOf/8`. Root cause: schema had been assembled from near-full local generations. Fixed by generating with true `--all-features` (which links now) and splicing in main's key order.\n   - **User feedback — commits authored by pawan-dt**: root cause was repo-local `user.email` plus CLAUDE.md's own instruction to \"switch back to pawan-dt\". Fixed identity, rewrote the rule, reauthored 21 commits, force-pushed with approval.\n   - **User feedback — 21k-line diff**: phantom diff from generated `$defs` reordering; fixed by preserving main's key order (10.8k → 622 lines).\n   - **User feedback — Co-authored-by trailers in merged commits**: confirmed in exactly 2 commits; documented cause + prevention; awaiting decision on rewriting published main history.\n   - **Agent `git stash` wiped the shared working tree**: my postgres-cdc SQLSTATE work was lost. Recovered via `git checkout stash@{0} -- crates/source/postgres-cdc/src/replication.rs`, re-applied the final one-line test edit, verified 114 tests pass, and audited all stashed files for other losses (none).\n   - **Agent introduced a major-version break** (removed `pub verify_length`/`verify_checksum`): overruled per the user's \"never bump a major\" rule; restored plain fields; semver clean.\n   - **`TokenError::new` not public** → extracted pure `classify_server_code(u32)` and tested that instead.\n   - **DuckDB qualified-column wording** (`Table \"b\" does not have a column named \"x\"`) missed by my first predicate — caught by the existing `http_relation` tests; added the wording.\n   - **`RestStream`/`SqliteHistory` lack `Debug`** → used `match`/`.err().expect()` instead of `unwrap_err`/`expect_err`.\n   - **Test insertion landed mid-function** (compile.rs has no test module) → `git checkout` the file, re-applied production fix only, put tests in `tests/runtime.rs`.\n   - **clippy `manual_is_multiple_of`** in a peer's `write_mode.rs` test → `.count().is_multiple_of(2)`.\n   - **Repeated ENOSPC**: freed 58 GB+ several times (`target/debug`, `target/debug/incremental`, `target/llvm-cov-target`, `~/.cargo/registry/cache`). Blocked again at the very end.\n   - **`gh auth` active account repeatedly drifts to pawan-dt** (pinned in `~/.config/gh/hosts.yml`): must combine `gh auth switch` + the operation in ONE command, use `gh auth token --user PawanSikawat`, and verify with `gh api user`.\n\n5. **Problem Solving:**\n   Completed: full-PR adversarial review with all findings fixed in-PR; coverage raised to 95% and gap closed to 97.25/97.47%; identity contamination eliminated from all commit *authors* and prevented structurally; phantom diff collapsed; MinIO Docker Hub withdrawal fixed repo-wide (PR #653, merged); whole-project principles audit filed as #654; correctness fixes shipped as #656 plus (in progress) all remaining non-breaking audit items.\n   Ongoing: #656 CI Coverage was at 89.95% (needed 10 more lines) — I closed all identified gaps (MSSQL pure decision table, delta typed test, pipeline premise assertions, unified HTTP retry arm) but had not yet re-measured/pushed. Disk exhaustion is actively blocking the final gate run.\n\n6. **All user messages:**\n   - \"Now tell me, have you done a review of the whole PR, and is there anything that you would change?\"\n   - \"contunue\"\n   - \"Are you stuck?\"\n   - \"ci failed on test coverage. can you please ensure always that we follow atleat 95% test coverage\"\n   - \"the commits are comming from pawan-dt. please dont do that\"\n   - \"Don't ever use the Pawan-DT git account on this repo. I'm being very, very clear. It should always use the other ID. I can't be more serious about it. Please don't ever use that.\"\n   - \"Yes, please do the push.\"\n   - \"why is this 21k lines of code now? it was 10k earlier\"\n   - \"based on the new principles we defined, evaluate the whole project and check whether there are any improvement areas or something we should fix\"\n   - \"you are the expert, wear an expert hat and a expert maintainer of this world class repo. take the right call which you should be certain about and do it\"\n   - \"Are there any fixes which are pending right now that you should solve?\"\n   - \"Please solve all of them in the same PR issues.\"\n   - \"https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/commit/6433e74b... https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/commit/fd32cf08... Both these commits have Pawan's detail inside them.\"\n   - \"pawan-dt\"\n   - (Also a `/model` command output switching to Opus 5 with \"continue\".)\n\n7. **Pending Tasks:**\n   - **Finish #656**: free disk, regenerate `schemas/faucet.schema.json` (config doc comments + restored field shapes changed it), run full-workspace `cargo fmt`/`clippy --all-targets --all-features -D warnings`, key test suites, re-measure patch coverage ≥95%, commit all ~68 files, push to `fix/audit-correctness-paths`.\n   - **Awaiting user decision**: whether to rewrite published `main` history (force-push) to strip the `Co-authored-by: pawan-dt` trailers from 6433e74b and fd32cf08. I explained it touches 3 commits, diverges all clones/forks, requires #656 to land or rebase first, and that trees stay byte-identical.\n   - **#654 backlog, deliberately deferred** (need user decisions; break YAML/API): H9 (`deny_unknown_fields` on 62 configs vs the `#[serde(flatten)]` tension), H10 (semver lints across 89 crates + widen CI beyond faucet-core), M20–M24 (flat-key-group regrouping, vocabulary renames, generic-machinery block-name hardcoding, async-job `query` path).\n   - **New issues suggested by agents but not yet filed**: kafka sink `headers_path` parsed but never applied to produced messages (bug/tier-2); `NodeReport.error` is `Option<String>` so per-node topology circuit-open isn't typed.\n   - #652 (value-path overwrite bookmark can outrun a failed `commit_overwrite`) remains open and unfixed by design.\n   - Task #33 (concurrency re-sweep) still ON HOLD.\n\n8. **Current Work:**\n   Immediately before this summary I was running the final gate sequence for PR #656 after all five parallel workstreams landed (~68 files touched). I had just:\n   - Overruled the agent-introduced major break by restoring `pub verify_length`/`pub verify_checksum` on s3/gcs/azure-blob, added `default_true()` to all three crates, and confirmed `cargo semver-checks check-release -p faucet-source-s3 --baseline-rev origin/main` → **\"Summary no semver update required\"** for both s3 and gcs.\n   - Confirmed workspace clippy clean (after fixing `SqliteHistory` Debug bound with `.err().expect()`), `faucet-cli --features full --lib` = 1632 passed, `faucet-core` all green, s3/gcs/azure = 41/45/50 passed.\n   - Then attempted `cargo fmt --all` + schema regeneration + `schema_config` test, which failed: `gen 101` and `write error: no space left on device`. My follow-up `rm -rf target/debug/incremental target/semver-checks target/doc` itself failed with `ENOSPC: no space left on device` when the harness tried to write the command's output file.\n\n9. **Optional Next Step:**\n   Free disk space (wipe `target/debug` and `target/llvm-cov-target`, which are fully regenerable), then complete the #656 gate sequence exactly as left off: regenerate `schemas/faucet.schema.json` with `cargo run -q -p faucet-cli --all-features -- schema config` spliced in the committed file's key order, verify `cargo test -p faucet-cli --all-features --test schema_config`, run `cargo fmt --all` + `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings`, re-measure patch coverage against the 95% floor, then commit and push to `fix/audit-correctness-paths` (author `PawanSikawat <pawansikawat1998@gmail.com>`, push via `gh auth token --user PawanSikawat` with the account verified in the same command).\n\n   This is directly in line with the user's instruction: **\"Please solve all of them in the same PR issues.\"**\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"90408eeb-03d6-4b1d-808c-1f54fc0f6b29","timestamp":"2026-09-17T12:50:40.183Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
