{"parentUuid":"23007497-c7e7-438c-ba7e-0f0449299e5e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14935866 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d8ca5a4b-a72f-491a-affb-e24d41610fdc","timestamp":"2026-09-17T14:02:42.070Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14935866 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"d8ca5a4b-a72f-491a-affb-e24d41610fdc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf98pV5E8gCrmokMwKV7z","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018fzQw8KuZmgtN5WkUG5mRa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix: replace the remaining message-grep classifications with typed ones\n\nCloses out the non-breaking half of the principles audit: every place that\ndecided control flow by matching a string is now keyed off a variant, a code,\nor a declared constant, and every place that copied core's retry jitter now\ncalls it.\n\nTyped classification (PRINCIPLES §6)\n- scheduler: circuit-open detection rides a new `InvocationErrorKind` carried\n  on `InvocationOutcome`, not the `CircuitOpen` display prefix, so rewording\n  the error can no longer silence the cooldown.\n- run history: `sql::classify_backend_error` decides transience from the\n  typed `sqlx::Error` (variant, then SQLSTATE / SQLite extended code) at the\n  one place the driver error is still intact; the startup connect now retries\n  a transient failure instead of degrading straight to the in-memory store.\n- graphql: request-rejection is decided from `extensions.code` alone; the\n  `batch_size = 0` non-null prose becomes a message hint rather than a\n  variant flip.\n- parquet: arrow decoder errors are classified by variant, so an allocation\n  failure is no longer reported as type drift.\n\nShared retry jitter (one implementation, five call sites)\n- kinesis source + kinesis/sqs sinks, grpc and websocket reconnects all\n  delegate to `faucet_core::retry::apply_jitter`. The kinesis source's fixed\n  per-shard fraction never broke a herd; websocket's fixed backoff redialled\n  a dead endpoint forever with no ceiling.\n\nReserved names get one definition\n- `CDC_DEFAULT_MARKER_FIELD`, `OVERWRITE_STAGING_SUFFIX(_OLD)`,\n  `UNCHANGED_TOAST_FIELD`; the CLI's `cdc_unwrap` decoder now uses core's\n  spec directly so its defaults cannot drift from the sink that matches them.\n\nAlso: `faucet_core::sql_literal` is public with the ANSI contract stated and\nClickHouse's divergent escaper documents why it must differ; unbalanced XML\nreturns a typed error instead of panicking on network input; `deny_unknown_fields`\non the kafka/kinesis/pubsub/sqs/databricks config blocks that lacked it; s3, gcs\nand azure-blob document both verify switches identically and validate them at\nload time.\n\nAddresses #654\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1; git log -1 --format='%an <%ae>'","description":"Commit the audit fixes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":364,"cache_read_input_tokens":269001,"output_tokens":1016,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":364,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1016,"cache_read_input_tokens":269001,"cache_creation_input_tokens":364,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":364},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018fzQw8KuZmgtN5WkUG5mRa":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix: replace the remaining message-grep classifications with typed ones\n\nCloses out the non-breaking half of the principles audit: every place that\ndecided control flow by matching a string is now keyed off a variant, a code,\nor a declared constant, and every place that copied core's retry jitter now\ncalls it.\n\nTyped classification (PRINCIPLES §6)\n- scheduler: circuit-open detection rides a new `InvocationErrorKind` carried\n  on `InvocationOutcome`, not the `CircuitOpen` display prefix, so rewording\n  the error can no longer silence the cooldown.\n- run history: `sql::classify_backend_error` decides transience from the\n  typed `sqlx::Error` (variant, then SQLSTATE / SQLite extended code) at the\n  one place the driver error is still intact; the startup connect now retries\n  a transient failure instead of degrading straight to the in-memory store.\n- graphql: request-rejection is decided from `extensions.code` alone; the\n  `batch_size = 0` non-null prose becomes a message hint rather than a\n  variant flip.\n- parquet: arrow decoder errors are classified by variant, so an allocation\n  failure is no longer reported as type drift.\n\nShared retry jitter (one implementation, five call sites)\n- kinesis source + kinesis/sqs sinks, grpc and websocket reconnects all\n  delegate to `faucet_core::retry::apply_jitter`. The kinesis source's fixed\n  per-shard fraction never broke a herd; websocket's fixed backoff redialled\n  a dead endpoint forever with no ceiling.\n\nReserved names get one definition\n- `CDC_DEFAULT_MARKER_FIELD`, `OVERWRITE_STAGING_SUFFIX(_OLD)`,\n  `UNCHANGED_TOAST_FIELD`; the CLI's `cdc_unwrap` decoder now uses core's\n  spec directly so its defaults cannot drift from the sink that matches them.\n\nAlso: `faucet_core::sql_literal` is public with the ANSI contract stated and\nClickHouse's divergent escaper documents why it must differ; unbalanced XML\nreturns a typed error instead of panicking on network input; `deny_unknown_fields`\non the kafka/kinesis/pubsub/sqs/databricks config blocks that lacked it; s3, gcs\nand azure-blob document both verify switches identically and validate them at\nload time.\n\nAddresses #654\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1; git log -1 --format='%an <%ae>'","description":"Commit