{"parentUuid":"9906d670-2871-49b4-929a-a08af8a37126","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14865046 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"37c0a0ce-9bfd-4eb7-a715-c10eda3aa397","timestamp":"2026-09-17T14:57:15.786Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14865046 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"37c0a0ce-9bfd-4eb7-a715-c10eda3aa397","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf9CyoPWwe1Kz5hHYp3WZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Local patch coverage came in at **90.20%** — below the 95% floor — but the shortfall is mostly measurement scope, not missing tests. Breaking down all 138 uncovered lines:\n\n| Lines | Where | Real gap? |\n|---|---|---|\n| 21 | `postgres-cdc/replication.rs` | No — live PG replication, CI runs it |\n| 18 | `mssql/sink.rs` | No — image is x86-only |\n| 17 | `graphql/stream.rs` | **Yes** — fixed |\n| 15 | `serve/history/sql.rs` | No — serve integration tests |\n| 13 | `sink/http` | No — `tests/coverage.rs` covers both retry arms; my run was `--lib` |\n| 9 | `azure-blob/stream.rs` | No — object-store integration |\n| 7+4+4 | websocket / grpc / decode | Mostly integration; the decode ones are near-unreachable by design |\n| 5 | `cli/src/topology.rs` | Integration |\n\nThe one I judged a genuine gap I fixed properly rather than by bolting on a wiremock test: `classify_graphql_errors` was pure and well-tested, but the 17 lines *using* it — sentinel derivation, hint composition, variant selection — sat inside the async fetch method, reachable only through a network round-trip. Extracted `sentinel_page_size_variable` + `graphql_error_from_payload` as pure functions and pinned all six branches with unit tests. That's the \"extract the pure logic rather than call it untestable\" move the policy asks for, and it's a better outcome than the coverage number it buys.\n\nThat commit is held locally so I don't restart the in-flight CI run. I'm now re-instrumenting the Docker-free crates with their **full** suites so my local figure stops understating what CI actually measures."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":727,"cache_read_input_tokens":339637,"output_tokens":611,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":727,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":611,"cache_read_input_tokens":339637,"cache_creation_input_tokens":727,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":727},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf9CynuVmeeR1ytCGE7QW","type":"assistant","uuid":"00eacda4-3bd4-4075-8213-b707a71f6625","timestamp":"2026-09-17T14:57:25.175Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
