{"parentUuid":"d2b1a8b4-0dae-4fe4-8d06-5ff2afb0a319","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf9EH59uJYb9jcnBAu55m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The repo was transferred to `faucet-hq` and my `origin` URL redirects — so the branch lives on `faucet-hq`, not a fork:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":460,"cache_read_input_tokens":373126,"output_tokens":1864,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":209},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":460,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1864,"cache_read_input_tokens":373126,"cache_creation_input_tokens":460,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":460},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cf9EH4budWx2TQM6CMR9S","type":"assistant","uuid":"21d8124b-5f00-46df-bdc3-7bd2a618d166","timestamp":"2026-09-17T15:14:21.483Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/cover-pure-decisions","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"21d8124b-5f00-46df-bdc3-7bd2a618d166","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf9EH59uJYb9jcnBAu55m","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01QbZcv9ydJpAY1e3ZnYwTJk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nS=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f/scratchpad\ncat > $S/pr2.md <<'BODY'\nFollow-up to #656. While measuring patch coverage locally I found three places where logic that is *conceptually pure* had been left inside an async I/O path, so every branch of it was reachable only through a network round-trip or a live database. In each case the fix is to move the logic, not to reach for a container — which is what the coverage policy asks for (\"extract the pure logic; make the I/O a thin, separately-covered shim\") and leaves the code better regardless of the number.\n\nNo behaviour change anywhere in this PR. `cargo semver-checks` reports \"no semver update required\".\n\n## 1. GraphQL — the whole `200`-with-`errors[]` decision\n\n`classify_graphql_errors` was already pure and thoroughly tested. But the 17 lines that *used* it were not: deriving the sentinel page-size variable, composing the `batch_size = 0` hint, and choosing between `FaucetError::Config` and `HttpStatus` all sat inside `fetch_page`.\n\nExtracted `sentinel_page_size_variable` and `graphql_error_from_payload`; the fetch path is now a single call. Six tests pin what previously needed wiremock:\n\n- the transport/config split, and that the endpoint and joined message land in the error;\n- the hint appears **only** when the sentinel is live, and prose still never flips the variant;\n- a typed config code composing with the hint;\n- offset pagination never yielding a sentinel variable (it sends no page-size variable, so a validation error naming one has another cause and must not be explained away);\n- an `errors[]` entry carrying no `message` field at all.\n\n## 2. `pg_err` — the point of the SQLSTATE fix, untested\n\n`pg_err` is what keeps a Postgres error's code recoverable after the hop into `FaucetError`; once the error is stringified the code is gone for good. Nothing tested it.\n\nNow pinned: context and message survive, a non-database error carries `None` rather than a guessed code, and `sqlstate_of` reads the code back only from the typed carrier. The load-bearing case is the last one — an error whose *text* reads `replication slot \"s\" is active for PID 42 (SQLSTATE 55006)` must **not** be treated as slot-active. That is precisely what the old string match did, and it is the regression this test would catch.\n\n## 3. `run_topology`'s summary mapping\n\nThe tail of `run_topology` flattened a `TopologyRun` into a `RunSummary` inline, so the row ordering, the per-node failure attribution (#459), and the deliberate `error_kind: None` were reachable only by standing up a graph.\n\nExtracted as `build_summary`. It takes the two pieces it needs rather than the whole `TopologyRun` — which is not just tidier, it is what makes it testable at all: `NodeReport` is `#[non_exhaustive]`, so no other crate can construct one. Four tests cover:\n\n- output sorted by node id — the source is a `HashMap`, so without the explicit sort the order varies run to run, and `faucet run --output json` prints it;\n- one row per failed node, attributed to that node rather than a flat `topology` row;\n- that a failure row reports zero records;\n- that `error_kind` stays `None` even for a message reading `Circuit open after 3 consecutive failures`. That one is deliberate: it pins #658's current behaviour, so the day that lands, this test is what changes rather than being silently contradicted.\n\n## Gates\n\n`cargo fmt --all`; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -D warnings`; `faucet-cli` lib 1663 passed, `faucet-source-graphql` 65, `faucet-source-postgres-cdc` 116, the committed-schema test 5; `cargo semver-checks check-release -p faucet-source-graphql --baseline-rev origin/main` → no semver update required.\n\nRefs #654, #658.\nBODY\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1 && gh pr create \\\n  --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --base main --head test/cover-pure-decisions \\\n  --title \"test: cover the three pure decisions that were only reachable through I/O\" \\\n  --body-file $S/pr2.md 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Open the follow-up PR on faucet-hq"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":460,"cache_read_input_tokens":373126,"output_tokens":1864,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":209},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":460,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1864,"cache_read_input_tokens":373126,"cache_creation_input_tokens":460,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":460},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01QbZcv9ydJpAY1e3ZnYwTJk":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nS=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f/scratchpad\ncat > $S/pr2.md <<'BODY'\nFollow-up to #656. While measuring patch coverage locally I found three places where logic that is *conceptually pure* had been left inside an async I/O path, so every branch of it was reachable only through a network round-trip or a live database. In each case the fix is to move the logic, not to reach for a container — which is what the coverage policy asks for (\"extract the pure logic; make the I/O a thin, separately-covered shim\") and leaves the code better regardless of the number.\n\nNo behaviour change anywhere in this PR. `cargo semver-checks` reports \"no semver update required\".\n\n## 1. GraphQL — the whole `200`-with-`errors[]` decision\n\n`classify_graphql_errors` was already pure and thoroughly tested. But the 17 lines that *used* it were not: deriving the sentinel page-size variable, composing the `batch_size = 0` hint, and choosing between `FaucetError::Config` and `HttpStatus` all sat inside `fetch_page`.\n\nExtracted `sentinel_page_size_variable` and `graphql_error_from_payload`; the fetch path is now a single call. Six tests pin what previously needed wiremock:\n\n- the transport/config split, and that the endpoint and joined message land in the error;\n- the hint appears **only** when the sentinel is live, and prose still never flips the variant;\n- a typed config code composing with the hint;\n- offset pagination never yielding a sentinel variable (it sends no page-size variable, so a validation error naming one has another cause and must not be explained away);\n- an `errors[]` entry carrying no `message` field at all.\n\n## 2. `pg_err` — the point of the SQLSTATE fix, untested\n\n`pg_err` is what keeps a Postgres error's code recoverable after the hop into `FaucetError`; once the error is stringified the code is gone for good. Nothing tested it.\n\nNow pinned: context and message survive, a non-database error carries `None` rather than a guessed code, and `sqlstate_of` reads the code back only from the typed carrier. The load-bearing case is the last one — an error whose *text* reads `replication slot \"s\" is active for PID 42 (SQLSTATE 55006)` must **not** be treated as slot-active. That is precisely what the old string match did, and it is the regression this test would catch.\n\n## 3. `run_topology`'s summary mapping\n\nThe tail of `run_topology` flattened a `TopologyRun` into a `RunSummary` inline, so the row ordering, the per-node failure attribution (#459), and the deliberate `error_kind: None` were reachable only by standing up a graph.\n\nExtracted as `build_summary`. It takes the two pieces it needs rather than the whole `TopologyRun` — which is not just tidier, it is what makes it testable at all: `NodeReport` is `#[non_exhaustive]`, so no other crate can construct one. Four tests cover:\n\n- output sorted by node id — the source is a `HashMap`, so without the explicit sort the order varies run to run, and `faucet run --output json` prints it;\n- one row per failed node, attributed to that node rather than a flat `topology` row;\n- that a failure row reports zero records;\n- that `error_kind` stays `None` even for a message reading `Circuit open after 3 consecutive failures`. That one is deliberate: it pins #658's current behaviour, so the day that lands, this test is what changes rather than being silently contradicted.\n\n## Gates\n\n`cargo fmt --all`; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -D warnings`; `faucet-cli` lib 1663 passed, `faucet-source-graphql` 65, `faucet-source-postgres-cdc` 116, the committed-schema test 5; `cargo semver-checks check-release -p faucet-source-graphql --baseline-rev origin/main` → no semver update required.\n\nRefs #654, #658.\nBODY\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1 && gh pr create \\\n  --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --base main --head test/cover-pure-decisions \\\n  --title \"test: cover the three pure decisions that were only reachable through I/O\" \\\n  --body-file $S/pr2.md 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Open the follow-up PR on faucet-hq"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cf9EH4budWx2TQM6CMR9S","type":"assistant","uuid":"5c9c49df-bdee-471b-9f65-3fa23956e2da","timestamp":"2026-09-17T15:14:34.439Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/cover-pure-decisions","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
