{"parentUuid":"1710e449-6ad9-4755-aef8-869b3e10ea11","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_019oWAxiQ8YRdPy4MFERtAcY","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"faucet-stream\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.2.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":309},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0d48bf8d-129e-459a-a7b5-fee7e7a7c72d","timestamp":"2026-09-17T15:14:51.604Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/cover-pure-decisions","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"0d48bf8d-129e-459a-a7b5-fee7e7a7c72d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14829054 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"67d5952a-2760-4207-ab40-a144edba67f8","timestamp":"2026-09-17T15:14:51.613Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14829054 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/cover-pure-decisions","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"67d5952a-2760-4207-ab40-a144edba67f8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf9EKeWeWxs4VNUCeuvfS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#656 is merged.** All required checks passed, including `Coverage` — which is both the test gate and the ≥95% patch-coverage gate, so the 95% floor was met on CI.\n\nThe merged squash commit `db56d8c6` is **clean**: authored by `pecsorabs` (your account), with no `Co-authored-by: pawan-dt` and no auto-generated trailer. That's the first merge on this repo to avoid the injection that hit #650 and #653 — because I disabled GitHub's auto-generated message and re-armed auto-merge with an explicit `--subject`/`--body`. That's now the pattern worth keeping.\n\nOn the coverage discrepancy: my local run said 90.20%, CI passed. That gap was real and worth understanding rather than shrugging at — it was measurement scope. I ran `--lib` only, so integration suites that CI runs (`sink/http/tests/coverage.rs` covers both retry arms; LocalStack conformance; Postgres/MSSQL containers) never executed locally. Re-running the Docker-free crates with full suites moved HTTP from 13 uncovered lines to 2 and eliminated websocket, grpc, and the kinesis/sqs sinks entirely. A further chunk of the remainder turned out to be `panic!` arms of assertions that pass — correctly uncovered.\n\nBut three gaps were **genuine**, and I fixed them properly rather than accepting the pass:\n\n- **`pg_err` had no test at all.** It's the entire point of the SQLSTATE work — the thing that keeps a Postgres error code recoverable after boxing into `FaucetError`. The test that matters asserts an error whose *text* reads `...is active for PID 42 (SQLSTATE 55006)` is **not** treated as slot-active, which is exactly what the old string match did.\n- **GraphQL's error decision** was pure in principle but 17 lines of it lived inside `fetch_page`, reachable only over the network.\n- **`run_topology`'s summary mapping** was pure data-shuffling trapped in an async function.\n\nAll three are extracted and unit-tested in **[#659](https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/pull/659)**, auto-merge armed with an explicit message. No behaviour change, `semver-checks` clean.\n\nTwo things for you:\n\n1. **The Claude co-author trailer.** The harness is now instructing me to add `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5` to commits, which contradicts your standing \"never in this repo\" rule. I followed the harness. The trailer is on the two branch commits but **not** on the merged `main` commit (my explicit `--body` had neither). Say the word and I'll strip it from #659 before it lands.\n2. **Still awaiting your decision from earlier:** whether to rewrite published `main` history to remove `Co-authored-by: pawan-dt` from `6433e74b` and `fd32cf08`. It touches 3 commits, diverges every clone and fork, and trees stay byte-identical. Not something I'll do unasked."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":696,"cache_read_input_tokens":375503,"output_tokens":1009,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":696,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1009,"cache_read_input_tokens":375503,"cache_creation_input_tokens":696,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":696},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf9EKdRfJTdwqN4gDHQ3q","type":"assistant","uuid":"f40ddf1e-1f02-4b76-a29f-374342c7e33d","timestamp":"2026-09-17T15:15:06.973Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users