persisted before the sink confirmed the data that bookmark claims.**\n149\t///\n150\t/// `records_claimed` maps a persisted bookmark to the number of records it\n151\t/// asserts are durable. A bookmark that claims more than had been confirmed at\n152\t/// the moment it was written is a data-loss bug: a resumed run starts after it\n153\t/// and the unconfirmed records are never read again.\n154\t///\n155\t/// This lives here, rather than inline in each test, so the *same* assertion\n156\t/// can be pointed at a deliberately-wrong event log — which is how the suites\n157\t/// prove the check can actually fail (see this module's tests).\n158\tpub fn assert_bookmarks_backed_by_writes(\n159\t    log: &EventLog,\n160\t    records_claimed: impl Fn(&Value) -> usize,\n161\t) {\n162\t    let mut confirmed = 0usize;\n163\t    for (i, event) in log.events().into_iter().enumerate() {\n164\t        match event {\n165\t            Event::Write(n) | Event::IdempotentWrite { records: n, .. } => confirmed += n,\n166\t            Event::StatePut { ref value, .. } => {\n167\t                let claimed = records_claimed(value);\n168\t                assert!(\n169\t                    claimed <= confirmed,\n170\t                    \"durability violated at event {i}: bookmark {value} claims {claimed} \\\n171\t                     records are durable, but only {confirmed} had been confirmed by the sink. \\\n172\t                     A resumed run would start after this bookmark and never re-read the \\\n173\t                     difference.\\nfull log: {:?}\",\n174\t                    log.events()\n175\t                );\n176\t            }\n177\t            _ => {}\n178\t        }\n179\t    }\n180\t}\n181\t\n182\t/// The boundary a script fails at.\n183\t///\n184\t/// Every variant names a real transition the engine makes, and each one is a\n185\t/// place a naive implementation gets the ordering wrong.\n\n... [770 lines truncated] ...\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
