{"parentUuid":"ef7d2a73-2e69-47fc-9fec-ad6025a848e7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf9tka3ePTcKNxxjZfH6M","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013YTTzpSFZNSxWEKpzPz44P","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\npython3 - <<'PY'\np=\"docs/contributing/testing.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"- **Integration tests** live in the crate's `tests/` directory. HTTP connectors\n  use [`wiremock`](https://docs.rs/wiremock); database/queue connectors use\n  [`testcontainers`](https://docs.rs/testcontainers) (these need Docker and are\n  CI-gated).\n\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"- **Integration tests** live in the crate's `tests/` directory. HTTP connectors\n  use [`wiremock`](https://docs.rs/wiremock); database/queue connectors use\n  [`testcontainers`](https://docs.rs/testcontainers) (these need Docker and are\n  CI-gated).\n\nThere is a third kind that is neither: the **engine guarantee suites** in\n`crates/conformance/tests/reliability_*.rs`. A guarantee like \"the bookmark is\npersisted only after the sink confirms\" is a property of the *order* in which\nthe engine calls two collaborators, which neither a pure unit test nor a\nper-connector test can observe. Those suites drive the real `Pipeline::run`\nagainst doubles that fail at one named boundary and assert on the recorded event\nsequence. They are Docker-free, run in seconds, and are a **required** CI check.\nSee [Reliability testing](../book/src/operations/reliability-testing.md) for the\ntier map and how to add a guarantee.\n\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new,1)\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"## Related\n\n- [Testing standards](../standards/testing.md)\"\"\",\"\"\"## Related\n\n- [Reliability testing](../book/src/operations/reliability-testing.md)\n- [Testing standards](../standards/testing.md)\"\"\",1)\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"cross-linked\")\nPY\nwhich mdbook >/dev/null 2>&1 && (cd docs/book && mdbook build 2>&1 | tail -4) || echo \"(mdbook not installed locally — CI docs job verifies)\"","description":"Cross-link and try building the book","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":500,"cache_read_input_tokens":509501,"output_tokens":811,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":500,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":811,"cache_read_input_tokens":509501,"cache_creation_input_tokens":500,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":500},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013YTTzpSFZNSxWEKpzPz44P":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\npython3 - <<'PY'\np=\"docs/contributing/testing.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"- **Integration tests** live in the crate's `tests/` directory. HTTP connectors\n  use [`wiremock`](https://docs.rs/wiremock); database/queue connectors use\n  [`testcontainers`](https://docs.rs/testcontainers) (these need Docker and are\n  CI-gated).\n\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"- **Integration tests** live in the crate's `tests/` directory. HTTP connectors\n  use [`wiremock`](https://docs.rs/wiremock); database/queue connectors use\n  [`testcontainers`](https://docs.rs/testcontainers) (these need Docker and are\n  CI-gated).\n\nThere is a third kind that is neither: the **engine guarantee suites** in\n`crates/conformance/tests/reliability_*.rs`. A guarantee like \"the bookmark is\npersisted only after the sink confirms\" is a property of the *order* in which\nthe engine calls two collaborators, which neither a pure unit test nor a\nper-connector test can observe. Those suites drive the real `Pipeline::run`\nagainst doubles that fail at one named boundary and assert on the recorded event\nsequence. They are Docker-free, run in seconds, and are a **required** CI check.\nSee [Reliability testing](../book/src/operations/reliability-testing.md) for the\ntier map and how to add a guarantee.\n\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new,1)\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"## Related\n\n- [Testing standards](../standards/testing.md)\"\"\",\"\"\"## Related\n\n- [Reliability testing](../book/src/operations/reliability-testing.md)\n- [Testing standards](../standards/testing.md)\"\"\",1)\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s)\nprint(\"cross-linked\")\nPY\nwhich mdbook >/dev/null 2>&1 && (cd docs/book && mdbook build 2>&1 | tail -4) || echo \"(mdbook not installed locally — CI docs job verifies)\"","description":"Cross-link and try building the book","timeout":300000}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf9tkZDXS7kQEq1hy9Xpy","type":"assistant","uuid":"9d16461b-bcc6-4a39-a822-eb265fbb175c","timestamp":"2026-09-17T23:38:58.584Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
