{"parentUuid":"0d4d5f51-96ba-46d1-9edb-ec878a748a9c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf9uybSx7Z4QBZomRpuCy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BRJPJWAaLwyaz1n3QeUGyb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\nTOKEN=$(gh auth token --user PawanSikawat)\ngit -c credential.helper= \\\n    -c \"credential.https://github.com.helper=!f() { echo username=PawanSikawat; echo password=$TOKEN; }; f\" \\\n    push origin test/reliability-program 2>&1 | tail -2\ngh pr comment 660 --body \"Added a second Category F pair (\\`crates/sink/jsonl/tests/fidelity.rs\\`, 5 tests), which turned out to matter more than a second data point.\n\nIt is the **control** for the category: a JSONL file has no schema, no column types and no affinity rules, so nothing can be excused as a destination limitation. The assertion carries *no tolerance at all* — and it passes. Every hazard class in the shared corpus lands byte-identical, including negative zero and the integer past 2^53.\n\nThat settles a question the SQLite pair could only assume. Since these values survive a schemaless destination exactly, the losses SQLite's auto-mapped path exhibits (\\`true\\`/\\`false\\` → \\`1\\`/\\`0\\`, negative zero losing its sign) are genuinely SQLite's type system rather than faucet's serialization. Without this pair, attributing them to SQLite would have been a guess.\n\nAlso covers three shapes a single-batch test misses: the wide flat record (what a typed destination receives), \\`pretty: true\\` framing, and a two-page write — a sink that re-serialized its whole buffer per flush could corrupt already-written rows.\n\nDocs now describe both reference pairs and when to reach for which.\n\nNote this push restarts CI; \\`Reliability guarantees\\` had already passed on the previous commit, confirming the new job reports and is therefore eligible for the branch-protection required set.\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Push and note the addition on the PR","timeout":420000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4454,"cache_read_input_tokens":570923,"output_tokens":750,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4454,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":750,"cache_read_input_tokens":570923,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4454,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4454},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BRJPJWAaLwyaz1n3QeUGyb":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\nTOKEN=$(gh auth token --user PawanSikawat)\ngit -c credential.helper= \\\n    -c \"credential.https://github.com.helper=!f() { echo username=PawanSikawat; echo password=$TOKEN; }; f\" \\\n    push origin test/reliability-program 2>&1 | tail -2\ngh pr comment 660 --body \"Added a second Category F pair (\\`crates/sink/jsonl/tests/fidelity.rs\\`, 5 tests), which turned out to matter more than a second data point.\n\nIt is the **control** for the category: a JSONL file has no schema, no column types and no affinity rules, so nothing can be excused as a destination limitation. The assertion carries *no tolerance at all* — and it passes. Every hazard class in the shared corpus lands byte-identical, including negative zero and the integer past 2^53.\n\nThat settles a question the SQLite pair could only assume. Since these values survive a schemaless destination exactly, the losses SQLite's auto-mapped path exhibits (\\`true\\`/\\`false\\` → \\`1\\`/\\`0\\`, negative zero losing its sign) are genuinely SQLite's type system rather than faucet's serialization. Without this pair, attributing them to SQLite would have been a guess.\n\nAlso covers three shapes a single-batch test misses: the wide flat record (what a typed destination receives), \\`pretty: true\\` framing, and a two-page write — a sink that re-serialized its whole buffer per flush could corrupt already-written rows.\n\nDocs now describe both reference pairs and when to reach for which.\n\nNote this push restarts CI; \\`Reliability guarantees\\` had already passed on the previous commit, confirming the new job reports and is therefore eligible for the branch-protection required set.\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Push and note the addition on the PR","timeout":420000}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf9uyauTfSbNY5Ym79kCU","type":"assistant","uuid":"1373b963-26fd-4180-940d-5c121e54baed","timestamp":"2026-09-17T23:55:03.852Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
