{"parentUuid":"d53ad670-1bab-47ae-8aa2-092cd23465af","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf9vEuz6bs4bwC5XryiFA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GkMffAPNCnUWq49NcYiB6X","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\npython3 - <<'PY'\np=\".claude/rules/architecture.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\nold=\"| `faucet-conformance` | `crates/conformance/` | Connector-SDK conformance test harness — `assert_*` helpers + maturity-tier scoring used by every connector's `tests/conformance.rs` |\"\nnew=(\"| `faucet-conformance` | `crates/conformance/` | Connector-SDK conformance test harness — `assert_*` helpers + maturity-tier scoring used by every connector's `tests/conformance.rs`, \"\n     \"plus two modules supporting the **engine-level reliability program** (#651): `scripted` (boundary-precise failure injection — a shared ordered `EventLog`, \"\n     \"`ScriptedSink`/`ScriptedStateStore` that fail at exactly one named `Boundary`, a per-page-bookmarked `PagedSource`, and `assert_bookmarks_backed_by_writes`, \"\n     \"so the *ordering* guarantees a pure-logic test cannot observe get asserted against the real `Pipeline::run`) and `fidelity` (the shared typed round-trip corpus \"\n     \"+ `Tolerance` + `assert_round_trip`, so each source↔sink pair inherits a type-exactness test). The reliability suites themselves live in \"\n     \"`crates/conformance/tests/reliability_*.rs` and `compat_state_format.rs` (frozen state fixtures under `tests/fixtures/state/`) and run in the required \"\n     \"`Reliability guarantees` CI job; see `docs/book/src/operations/reliability-testing.md` |\")\nassert old in s\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s.replace(old,new,1))\nprint(\"architecture.md updated\")\nPY\npython3 - <<'PY'\n# maintenance.md: add the trigger row so future changes keep these in sync.\np=\".claude/rules/maintenance.md\"\ns=open(p).read()\nanchor=\"| **Add a dependency that introduces a new license** |\"\nrow=(\"| **Change an engine guarantee, or add a `Sink`/`Source` lifecycle hook (#651)** | the matching suite under `crates/conformance/tests/reliability_*.rs` \"\n     \"(and a new `Boundary`/`Event` in `crates/conformance/src/scripted.rs` if the failure point is new — plus a `#[should_panic]` proof that any reusable \"\n     \"assertion can still fail); the tier table + \\\"what each suite asserts\\\" section in `docs/book/src/operations/reliability-testing.md`; the `reliability` \"\n     \"job in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` if a new package needs covering; a frozen fixture under `crates/conformance/tests/fixtures/state/` when a new \"\n     \"**state shape** ships (never edit an existing one to make a test pass) |\\n\")\nassert anchor in s and \"reliability_*.rs\" not in s\nopen(p,\"w\").write(s.replace(anchor, row+anchor, 1))\nprint(\"maintenance.md updated\")\nPY\ngrep -c \"reliability\" .claude/rules/architecture.md .claude/rules/maintenance.md","description":"Update the architecture and maintenance rules"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1141,"cache_read_input_tokens":581382,"output_tokens":1164,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1141,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1164,"cache_read_input_tokens":581382,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1141,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1141},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01GkMffAPNCnUWq49NcYiB6X":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\npython3 - <<'PY'\np=\".claude/rules/architect