removed) before we mean to stop it.\n        container\n    });''',1)\ns=s.replace('''        Ok(result) => panic!(\n            \"the run reported SUCCESS after its connection was cut, having written {} of \\\\\n             40000 rows — a truncated dataset presented as complete is the worst outcome \\\\\n             available here\",\n            result.records_written\n        ),''','''        Ok(result) => panic!(\n            \"the run reported SUCCESS after its connection was cut, having written {} of \\\\\n             {total} rows — a truncated dataset presented as complete is the worst outcome \\\\\n             available here\",\n            result.records_written\n        ),''',1)\ns=s.replace('''    let written = sink.len();\n    assert!(\n        written < 40_000,\n        \"the read was supposed to be cut short, but {written} rows arrived\"\n    );''','''    let written = sink.len();\n    assert!(\n        (written as i64) < total,\n        \"the read was supposed to be cut short, but all {written} rows arrived\"\n    );''',1)\n\n# 3. Bookmark test: same slow source.\ns=s.replace('''    let (container, url) = start_postgres().await;\n    seed(&url, 40_000).await;\n\n    let src = source(&url, 100).await;\n    let sink = TestSink::new();\n\n    let killer = tokio::spawn(async move {\n        tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(400)).await;\n        container.stop().await.expect(\"stop\");\n        container\n    });''','''    let (container, url) = start_postgres().await;\n    let total = 3_000;\n    seed(&url, total).await;\n\n    let src = slow_source(&url, 100).await;\n    let sink = TestSink::new();\n\n    let killer = tokio::spawn(async move {\n        tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_millis(1_500)).await;\n        container.stop().await.expect(\"stop\");\n        container\n    });''',1)\n\n# 4. Connect-time test: the failure happens in `new()`, classified Config. Assert the real behaviour.\ns=s.replace('''#[tokio::test]\nasync fn a_cut_bef