{"parentUuid":"c5cadf5b-f879-45f8-bf4c-5c7f21200021","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14918976 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f2428ba7-0248-482c-aacd-118fbe9379e7","timestamp":"2026-09-18T05:08:28.070Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14918976 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/reliability-job-always-runs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"f2428ba7-0248-482c-aacd-118fbe9379e7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAKtaADinUczeKvAhdsR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0176NYyunswBJS7RC8ipXoCQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngit checkout -q -b test/reliability-program-phase2 origin/main\ngit add crates docs\ngit status --porcelain | head -12\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\ntest: finish the reliability program — drift matrix, 4 fidelity pairs, container faults\n\nCloses out every remaining #651 item. Nothing deferred.\n\n**A6 — the drift-policy matrix (8 tests, Docker-free, required tier).** `core::drift`\nunit-tests the classification and each sink tests its own `evolve_schema`; neither\ncovered what an operator actually configures. All five `on_drift` arms now run\nthrough the real pipeline against a destination that genuinely evolves, because\neach has a different silent wrong answer: `warn` dropping the page, `evolve`\nwriting without the DDL, `quarantine` writing the drifting rows anyway, `fail`\nwriting and *then* raising. Plus the control that a matching page is untouched by\nevery policy, and that `quarantine` without a DLQ is refused before data moves —\nwhich is a config-time gate, found because the control arm failed without one.\n\n**F — four more fidelity pairs (18 tests).** Together they establish more than\nindividually:\n\n- **jsonl** — exactly lossless, zero tolerance. The control: no schema, so no\n  excuse. Every hazard class survives, `-0.0` and the i64 past 2^53 included.\n- **postgres** — typed columns fully faithful (`DOUBLE PRECISION` keeps the sign\n  bit); JSONB does *not*, because it normalises through `numeric`, which has no\n  signed zero. So \"Postgres loses negative zero\" is false in general and true for\n  the document path. A dedicated test asserts both halves of that contrast rather\n  than leaving it in a comment.\n- **mysql** — typed columns faithful; backslashes survive despite MySQL treating\n  them as escapes, confirming the sink binds parameters rather than building\n  literals.\n- **mongodb** — BSON fully faithful with zero tolerance, `-0.0` included, and a\n  large integer is stored as Int64 rather than Double (asserted via canonical\n  extended JSON, so the chosen BSON *type* is checked, not just the value).\n\n**E1 — the container tier (5 tests).** Stops the database while a cursor is open:\na harder cut than a proxy toxic, since the socket dies with no FIN, and it needs\nno extra image. The run must fail rather than report success on partial data,\nterminate inside a hard ceiling, and never hand back a bookmark it cannot back.\n\nThe read is slowed deterministically with `pg_sleep` per row rather than by tuning\na delay — the first version raced, the table streamed in before the cut, and it\n\"failed\" against a perfectly healthy run.\n\n**Found on the way, filed as #662:** nine SQL sources type runtime query and\nconnection failures as `FaucetError::Config` — the variant meaning \"your YAML is\nwrong\" — when the config was fine and the database went away. Today that is a\ndiagnostics bug (`is_retriable()` is false for both variants, so nothing retries\ndifferently), but it becomes a reliability bug the moment a dropped connection is\nmade retriable, since `Config` is the one variant that must never be. The test\nasserts the guarantee that holds regardless and flags the variant, so it tightens\nwhen #662 lands instead of entrenching the defect.\n\nAlso: `Reliability guarantees` is now in the branch-protection required set, added\nafter #661 made the job always report.\n\nRefs #651, #662\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit phase 2 of the program"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1799,"cache_read_input_tokens":684632,"output_tokens":1325,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1799,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1325,"cache_read_input_tokens":684632,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1799,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1799},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0176NYyunswBJS7RC8ipXoCQ":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngit checkout -q -b test/reliability-program-phase2 origin/main\ngit add crates docs\ngit status --porcelain | head -12\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\ntest: finish the reliability program — drift matrix, 4 fidelity pairs, container faults\n\nCloses out every remaining #651 item. Nothing deferred.\n\n**A6 — the drift-policy matrix (8 tests, Docker-free, required tier).** `core::drift`\nunit-tests the classification and each sink tests its own `evolve_schema`; neither\ncovered what an operator actually configures. All five `on_drift` arms now run\nthrough the real pipeline against a destination that genuinely evolves, because\neach has a different silent wrong answer: `warn` dropping the page, `evolve`\nwriting without the DDL, `quarantine` writing the drifting rows anyway, `fail`\nwriting and *then* raising. Plus the control that a matching page is untouched by\nevery policy, and that `quarantine` without a DLQ is refused before data moves —\nwhich is a config-time gate, found because the control arm failed without one.\n\n**F — four more fidelity pairs (18 tests).** Together they establish more than\nindividually:\n\n- **jsonl** — exactly lossless, zero tolerance. The control: no schema, so no\n  excuse. Every hazard class survives, `-0.0` and the i64 past 2^53 included.\n- **postgres** — typed columns fully faithful (`DOUBLE PRECISION` keeps the sign\n  bit); JSONB does *not*, because it normalises through `numeric`, which has no\n  signed zero. So \"Postgres loses negative zero\" is false in general and true for\n  the document path. A dedicated test asserts both halves of that contrast rather\n  than leaving it in a comment.\n- **mysql** — typed columns faithful; backslashes survive despite MySQL treating\n  them as escapes, confirming the sink binds parameters rather than building\n  literals.\n- **mongodb** — BSON fully faithful with zero tolerance, `-0.0` included, and a\n  large integer is stored as Int64 rather than Double (asserted via canonical\n  extended JSON, so the chosen BSON *type* is checked, not just the value).\n\n**E1 — the container tier (5 tests).** Stops the database while a cursor is open:\na harder cut than a proxy toxic, since the socket dies with no FIN, and it needs\nno extra image. The run must fail rather than report success on partial data,\nterminate inside a hard ceiling, and never hand back a bookmark it cannot back.\n\nThe read is slowed deterministically with `pg_sleep` per row rather than by tuning\na delay — the first version raced, the table streamed in before the cut, and it\n\"failed\" against a perfectly healthy run.\n\n**Found on the way, filed as #662:** nine SQL sources type runtime query and\nconnection failures as `FaucetError::Config` — the variant meaning \"your YAML is\nwrong\" — when the config was fine and the database went away. Today that is a\ndiagnostics bug (`is_retriable()` is false for both variants, so nothing retries\ndifferently), but it becomes a reliability bug the moment a dropped connection is\nmade retriable, since `Config` is the one variant that must never be. The test\nasserts the guarantee that holds regardless and flags the variant, so it tightens\nwhen #662 lands instead of entrenching the defect.\n\nAlso: `Reliability guarantees` is now in the branch-protection required set, added\nafter #661 made the job always report.\n\nRefs #651, #662\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit phase 2 of the program"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfAKtZVHLMbHm5J4dpk1Z","type":"assistant","uuid":"42df9fcb-b473-4d6e-abcd-1a7139267a75","timestamp":"2026-09-18T05:08:45.228Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/reliability-job-always-runs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
