{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","prNumber":663,"prUrl":"https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/pull/663","prRepository":"faucet-hq/faucet-stream","timestamp":"2026-09-18T05:11:24.934Z"}
{"parentUuid":"ab965074-9cc6-4c2a-b7ec-0c5d5d820d83","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAL7bqYCKoK6cV8Yp4oG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is done. **[#663](https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/pull/663)** is up with `Closes #651`, auto-merge armed.\n\n**Branch protection is live** — `Reliability guarantees` is now required, added via the granular `PATCH` so all eight existing contexts survived.\n\n**The remaining three items, all built:**\n\n**A6 drift matrix** (8 tests, Docker-free, required tier) — all five `on_drift` arms through the real pipeline. Two tests came from doing the work rather than planning it: a control proving a *non-drifting* page is untouched by every policy, and `quarantine` without a DLQ being refused before data moves. I only found the latter because the control arm failed without one.\n\n**F fidelity** — four more destinations, and together they say more than individually:\n\n| | Result |\n|---|---|\n| jsonl | Exactly lossless, **zero tolerance** — the control |\n| postgres | Typed columns **fully faithful**, `-0.0` included; JSONB is not |\n| mysql | Faithful; backslashes survive (binds params, not literals) |\n| mongodb | BSON **fully faithful**; large ints stored as Int64, not Double |\n\nThe Postgres finding is the one worth knowing: JSONB normalises numbers through `numeric`, which has no signed zero. So **\"Postgres loses negative zero\" is false in general and true only for the document path.** One test writes the same `-0.0` to both a `DOUBLE PRECISION` and a JSONB column in one row and asserts both outcomes, so that's pinned rather than folklore.\n\n**E1 container tier** (5 tests) — stops the database mid-cursor, a harder cut than a proxy toxic and with no extra image needed.\n\nTwo things about how these got written that matter more than the counts:\n\n- My first fault-injection test **raced**: 40k rows streamed in before the 400ms cut, so it \"failed\" against a perfectly healthy run. I made the server the bottleneck with `pg_sleep` rather than tuning the delay — removing the timing assumption instead of hiding it.\n- MongoDB's integer test reads back as *canonical* extended JSON so the chosen BSON **type** is asserted (`$numberLong`), not just the value. A `Double` holding a small integer passes a value-only check and then loses digits on the first number past 2^53.\n\n**Filed [#662](https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/662)** from the container tier: nine SQL sources type runtime query/connection failures as `FaucetError::Config` — \"your YAML is wrong\" — when the database went away. I checked the blast radius before filing: `is_retriable()` is false for both variants, so it changes no retry behaviour *today*. It's a diagnostics bug that sends an on-call engineer to the wrong place, and becomes a reliability bug the moment dropped connections are made retriable, since `Config` is the one variant that must never be. I didn't fix it here — changing an error variant across nine crates deserves its own review — and the test asserts what holds regardless while flagging the variant, so it tightens when #662 lands rather than entrenching the defect.\n\nOn the B/C/D duplicates: I've still not written those, because my audit found the coverage genuinely exists across 292 files. If \"don't leave anything on the table\" meant those too, say so and I'll add them — but I'd be writing second tests for behaviour already tested, and I'd rather you decide that knowingly."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":604,"cache_read_input_tokens":692301,"output_tokens":1142,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":604,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1142,"cache_read_input_tokens":692301,"cache_creation_input_tokens":604,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":604},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfAL7b9rYx6NaBfSCisaK","type":"assistant","uuid":"266e5803-063f-4385-b2d3-cb9784fc9476","timestamp":"2026-09-18T05:11:40.363Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program-phase2","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
