{"parentUuid":"5deddf6a-e168-43d0-a8b5-c397e2ad3b29","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e0f7f418-adf2-4227-9df5-4e6afef6b88f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RP4rErrZAddzsqyvM8MdJT","type":"tool_result","content":"=== 640: REST dataset_uri today:\n2219:    fn dataset_uri(&self) -> String {\n2220-        let base = format!(\n2221-            \"{}{}\",\n2222-            faucet_core::redact_uri_credentials(&self.config.base_url),\n2223-            self.config.path\n2224-        );\n2225-        // Async-job sources (Salesforce Bulk etc.) address every object through the\n2226-        // *same* endpoint — the object lives in the SOQL query body, not the URL. So\n2227-        // without this, a 21-object matrix collapses to one catalog/lineage dataset\n2228-        // (#640). Derive a per-object URI from the query: the `FROM <SObject>` when\n2229-        // parseable, else a stable hash of the submit body (distinct query → distinct\n2230-        // dataset either way).\n2231-        if let Some(job) = &self.config.async_job {\n2232-            let sep = if base.ends_with('/') { \"\" } else { \"/\" };\n2233-            if let Some(obj) = async_job_object(job.submit.json.as_ref()) {\n2234-                return format!(\"{base}{sep}objects/{obj}\");\n2235-            }\n2236-            if let Some(j) = &job.submit.json {\n2237-                // FNV-1a from core (stable across Rust releases — this feeds persisted\n2238-                // catalog/lineage identity, so `DefaultHasher` would re-key it on a\n2239-                // toolchain bump).\n2240-                return format!(\n2241-                    \"{base}{sep}job/{:016x}\",\n--\n3061:    fn dataset_uri_combines_base_and_path() {\n3062-        use faucet_core::Source;\n\n=== was that the #650 change?\nfd32cf08 feat: generic REST discovery, partitioned typed OData, byte-passthrough loads + BigQuery/serve upgrades (#650)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fab80503-13e0-42b6-a852-e6f