{"parentUuid":"43300d9b-4dce-4b50-9bc5-d78afe0529fd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAXZd7vqJMKYuQuh2wFs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Audit complete. Let me close the four that are already fixed, with evidence:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":776,"cache_read_input_tokens":726862,"output_tokens":2514,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":960},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":776,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2514,"cache_read_input_tokens":726862,"cache_creation_input_tokens":776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":776},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfAXZcYTCU8aL4q9oRe8Q","type":"assistant","uuid":"b018d8cc-43f4-4a7f-8dcc-aa2da531ccec","timestamp":"2026-09-18T07:41:48.926Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program-phase2","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"b018d8cc-43f4-4a7f-8dcc-aa2da531ccec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAXZd7vqJMKYuQuh2wFs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DtqbRZdR2qrjViq4SG1nsw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\nclose() {\n  gh issue comment \"$1\" --body \"$2\" >/dev/null && gh issue close \"$1\" --reason completed >/dev/null && echo \"closed #$1\"\n}\nclose 611 \"Already fixed — landed in #650 (\\`fd32cf08\\`) without a closing keyword, so this stayed open.\n\nBoth \\`tables.get\\` call sites now pass \\`None\\` rather than \\`Some(vec![\\\"schema\\\"])\\`, which is exactly the fix this issue prescribes:\n\n\\`\\`\\`rust\n// crates/sink/bigquery/src/sink.rs:731 — fetch_schema_fields\nself.client.table().get(&project_id, &dataset_id, &table_id, None)\n// crates/sink/bigquery/src/sink.rs:1377 — table_exists\nself.client.table().get(&project_id, &dataset_id, table_id, None)\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nVerified by \\`git log -S 'vec![\\\"schema\\\"]'\\`: the last commit touching that literal is \\`fd32cf08\\`.\n\nOne loose end I'll tidy separately: \\`table_exists\\`'s comment still reads \\\"Request the \\`schema\\` field (as \\`fetch_schema_fields\\` does)\\\", which is now stale — it passes \\`None\\`.\"\nclose 613 \"Already fixed — landed in #650 (\\`fd32cf08\\`) without a closing keyword.\n\n\\`TransformingSource::stream_pages\\` no longer shrinks a source's page to the pipeline hint:\n\n\\`\\`\\`rust\n// crates/core/src/transforming_source.rs:155\nlet effective = std::cmp::max(batch_size, page_len);\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nwith the surrounding comments naming the source's own \\`batch_size\\` as \\\"the authoritative knob\\\" and citing the 200k-row-page-shrunk-to-1000 case this issue reported. The \\`batch_size == 0\\` sentinel is handled separately just above.\n\nVerified by \\`git log -S 'std::cmp::max(batch_size, page_len)'\\`.\"\nclose 627 \"Already fixed — landed in #650 (\\`fd32cf08\\`) without a closing keyword.\n\nThe token endpoint now supports form encoding, selected by \\`TokenBodyEncoding\\`:\n\n\\`\\`\\`rust\n// crates/source/rest/src/auth/token_endpoint.rs:262\nTokenBodyEncoding::Form => req.form(&form_pairs(b)?),\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nThere is also a wiremock test asserting the header, so the behaviour is pinned rather than incidental:\n\n\\`\\`\\`rust\n// token_endpoint.rs:751\n.and(header(\\\"content-type\\\", \\\"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\\\"))\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n\\`faucet-auth\\`'s own flows (\\`flow.rs:686\\`, \\`oauth2.rs:94\\`) already used \\`.form(..)\\`.\"\nclose 640 \"Already fixed — landed in #650 (\\`fd32cf08\\`) without a closing keyword. The implementation even cites this issue number in its comment.\n\n\\`RestStream::dataset_uri\\` now derives a per-object URI for async-job sources instead of returning the shared endpoint:\n\n\\`\\`\\`rust\n// crates/source/rest/src/stream.rs:2231\nif let Some(job) = &self.config.async_job {\n    if let Some(obj) = async_job_object(job.submit.json.as_ref()) {\n        return format!(\\\"{base}{sep}objects/{obj}\\\");   // FROM <SObject>\n    }\n    // else a stable FNV-1a hash of the submit body\n    return format!(\\\"{base}{sep}job/{:016x}\\\", ...);\n}\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nThat matches the proposed design: the \\`FROM <SObject>\\` when parseable, else a distinct-query-distinct-dataset hash. FNV-1a from core was used deliberately rather than \\`DefaultHasher\\`, since this feeds persisted catalog/lineage identity and would otherwise re-key on a toolchain bump.\n\nSQL sources were already differentiated — e.g. \\`postgres/stream.rs:376\\` returns \\`{url}?query={query}\\`.\"","description":"Close the four already-fixed bugs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":776,"cache_read_input_tokens":726862,"output_tokens":2514,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":960},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":776,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2514,"cache_read_input_tokens":726862,"cache_creation_input_tokens":776,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":776},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01DtqbRZdR2qrjViq4SG1nsw":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\nclose() {\n  gh issue comment \"$1\" --body \"$2\" >/dev/null && gh issue close \"$1\" --reason completed >/dev/null && echo \"closed #$1\"\n}\nclose 611 \"Already fixed — landed in #650 (\\`fd32cf08\\`) without a closing keyword, so this stayed open.\n\nBoth \\`tables.get\\` call sites now pass \\`None\\` rather than \\`Some(vec![\\\"schema\\\"])\\`, which is exactly the fix this issue prescribes:\n\n\\`\\`\\`rust\n// crates/sink/bigquery/src/sink.rs:731 — fetch_schema_fields\nself.client.table().get(&project_id, &dataset_id, &table_id, None)\n// crates/sink/bigquery/src/sink.rs:1377 — table_exists\nself.client.table().get(&project_id, &dataset_id, table_id, None)\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nVerified by \\`git log -S 'vec![\\\"schema\\\"]'\\`: the last commit touching that literal is \\`fd32cf08\\`.\n\nOne loose end I'll tidy separately: \\`table_exists\\`'s comment still reads \\\"Request the \\`schema\\` field (as \\`fetch_schema_fields\\` does)\\\", which is now stale — it passes \\`None\\`.\"\nclose 613 \"Already fixed — landed in #650 (\\`fd32cf08\\`) without a closing keyword.\n\n\\`TransformingSource::stream_pages\\` no longer shrinks a source's page to the pipeline hint:\n\n\\`\\`\\`rust\n// crates/core/src/transforming_source.rs:155\nlet effective = std::cmp::max(batch_size, page_len);\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nwith the surrounding comments naming the source's own \\`batch_size\\` as \\\"the authoritative knob\\\" and citing the 200k-row-page-shrunk-to-1000 case this issue reported. The \\`batch_size == 0\\` sentinel is handled separately just above.\n\nVerified by \\`git log -S 'std::cmp::max(batch_size, page_len)'\\`.\"\nclose 627 \"Already fixed — landed in #650 (\\`fd32cf08\\`) without a closing keyword.\n\nThe token endpoint now supports form encoding, selected by \\`TokenBodyEncoding\\`:\n\n\\`\\`\\`rust\n// crates/source/rest/src/auth/token_endpoint.rs:262\nTokenBodyEncoding::Form => req.form(&form_pairs(b)?),\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nThere is also a wiremock test asserting the header, so the behaviour is pinned rather than incidental:\n\n\\`\\`\\`rust\n// token_endpoint.rs:751\n.and(header(\\\"content-type\\\", \\\"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\\\"))\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n\\`faucet-auth\\`'s own flows (\\`flow.rs:686\\`, \\`oauth2.rs:94\\`) already used \\`.form(..)\\`.\"\nclose 640 \"Already fixed — landed in #650 (\\`fd32cf08\\`) without a closing keyword. The implementation even cites this issue number in its comment.\n\n\\`RestStream::dataset_uri\\` now derives a per-object URI for async-job sources instead of returning the shared endpoint:\n\n\\`\\`\\`rust\n// crates/source/rest/src/stream.rs:2231\nif let Some(job) = &self.config.async_job {\n    if let Some(obj) = async_job_object(job.submit.json.as_ref()) {\n        return format!(\\\"{base}{sep}objects/{obj}\\\");   // FROM <SObject>\n    }\n    // else a stable FNV-1a hash of the submit body\n    return format!(\\\"{base}{sep}job/{:016x}\\\", ...);\n}\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nThat matches the proposed design: the \\`FROM <SObject>\\` when parseable, else a distinct-query-distinct-dataset hash. FNV-1a from core was used deliberately rather than \\`DefaultHasher\\`, since this feeds persisted catalog/lineage identity and would otherwise re-key on a toolchain bump.