{"parentUuid":"21207d4b-0fed-4476-9736-5c403c105a46","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAaUnh7JHD1c29jDBttN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Clippy clean, whole Kafka suite green. Let me commit #657:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":738,"cache_read_input_tokens":793353,"output_tokens":1128,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":738,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1128,"cache_read_input_tokens":793353,"cache_creation_input_tokens":738,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":738},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfAaUmzSb3KqGNBPJiyU8","type":"assistant","uuid":"43a610e9-e17f-499b-b2f7-a527cd40a74b","timestamp":"2026-09-18T08:19:50.203Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/overwrite-bookmark-ordering","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"43a610e9-e17f-499b-b2f7-a527cd40a74b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAaUnh7JHD1c29jDBttN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VBLg2kTQgtRhPxZDyKkLbc","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nTOOL=~/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin\nexport PATH=$TOOL:$PATH RUSTC=$TOOL/rustc CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0\ncargo fmt --all\ncargo semver-checks check-release -p faucet-sink-kafka --baseline-rev origin/main 2>&1 | grep -Ei \"summary|required\" | head -2\ngit add crates/sink/kafka\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(sink-kafka): actually attach headers_path to the produced message\n\n`headers_path` was accepted by the config, extracted by a tested helper, and\ndocumented as producing Kafka headers — and then dropped on the floor. Nothing\nin either produce path attached it, so a config asking for headers produced\nmessages with none: no error, no warning, and a consumer routing on a header\nsimply saw nothing (#657).\n\nWired on both paths. The data record carries the headers; the exactly-once\ncommit-token record deliberately does not — it is faucet's own watermark on its\nown side-topic, not user data.\n\nA JSON `null` now becomes a **valueless** header rather than the string\n`\"null\"`. Kafka's header model permits no value, and that is the honest\nrendering: `\"null\"` is indistinguishable, to a consumer, from the\nfour-character string. `headers_at` therefore preserves `Value::Null` instead\nof stringifying it (everything else still stringifies). No existing test\nasserted the old behaviour, so nothing was rewritten to fit.\n\nFailure policy matches `partition_path`: a path resolving to nothing yields no\nheaders, and one resolving to a non-object fails the batch. A header map the\noperator asked for and did not get is not something to paper over.\n\nThe three per-record routing values now travel as a `RecordRouting` struct\nrather than three more positional `Option`s — clippy's arity limit was the\nprompt, but eight positional parameters (three of them `Option`) was the real\nproblem, and a caller swapping two would have built a subtly wrong message.\n\nFive integration tests consume the messages back and read their headers, so the\nassertions are about what reached the broker rather than what the extractor\nreturned. Getting them to run taught two things worth the comments they now\ncarry: `rdkafka`'s `StreamConsumer` polls on a background task, so a\ncurrent-thread runtime never receives anything; and the first `recv()` also pays\nfor the consumer group's JoinGroup/SyncGroup rebalance, so a short timeout gives\nup mid-rebalance and reports an empty topic — indistinguishable from \"the sink\nproduced nothing\", which is exactly how this suite first appeared to fail.\n\nREADME and config docs corrected — they previously advertised the gap.\n\nCloses #657\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -2","description":"Commit the kafka headers fix","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":738,"cache_read_input_tokens":793353,"output_tokens":1128,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":738,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1128,"cache_read_input_tokens":793353,"cache_creation_input_tokens":738,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":738},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VBLg2kTQgtRhPxZDyKkLbc":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nTOOL=~/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin\nexport PATH=$TOOL:$PATH RUSTC=$TOOL/rustc CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0\ncargo fmt --all\ncargo semver-checks check-release -p faucet-sink-kafka --baseline-rev origin/main 2>&1 | grep -Ei \"summary|required\" | head -2\ngit add crates/sink/kafka\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(sink-kafka): actually attach headers_path to the produced message\n\n`headers_path` was accepted by the config, extracted by a tested helper, and\ndocumented as producing Kafka headers — and then dropped on the floor. Nothing\nin either produce path attached it, so a config asking for headers produced\nmessages with none: no error, no warning, and a consumer routing on a header\nsimply saw nothing (#657).\n\nWired on both paths. The data record carries the headers; the exactly-once\ncommit-token record deliberately does not — it is faucet's own watermark on its\nown side-topic, not user data.\n\nA JSON `null` now becomes a **valueless** header rather than the string\n`\"null\"`. Kafka's header model permits no value, and that is the honest\nrendering: `\"null\"` is indistinguishable, to a consumer, from the\nfour-character string. `headers_at` therefore preserves `Value::Null` instead\nof stringifying it (everything else still stringifies). No existing test\nasserted the old behaviour, so nothing was rewritten to fit.\n\nFailure policy matches `partition_path`: a path resolving to nothing yields no\nheaders, and one resolving to a non-object fails the batch. A header map the\noperator asked for and did not get is not something to paper over.\n\nThe three per-record routing values now travel as a `RecordRouting` struct\nrather than three more positional `Option`s — clippy's arity limit was the\nprompt, but eight positional parameters (three of them `Option`) was the real\nproblem, and a caller swapping two would have built a subtly wrong message.\n\nFive integration tests consume the messages back and read their headers, so the\nassertions are about what reached the broker rather than what the extractor\nreturned. Getting them to run taught two things worth the comments they now\ncarry: `rdkafka`'s `StreamConsumer` polls on a background task, so a\ncurrent-thread runtime never receives anything; and the first `recv()` also pays\nfor the consumer group's JoinGroup/SyncGroup rebalance, so a short timeout gives\nup mid-rebalance and reports an empty topic — indistinguishable from \"the sink\nproduced nothing\", which is exactly how this suite first appeared to fail.\n\nREADME and config docs corrected — they previously advertised the gap.\n\nCloses #657\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -2","description":"Commit the kafka headers fix","timeout":900000}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfAaUmzSb3KqGNBPJiyU8","type":"assistant","uuid":"5f14c93a-b9fb-4b9a-aeb4-0536c2c99dad","timestamp":"2026-09-18T08:20:03.338Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/overwrite-bookmark-ordering","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
